# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 1: End-of-circuit detection {#part-1-end-of-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "Bagian 1: Deteksi di akhir circuit {#part-1-end-of-circuit-detection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Part 1, we focus on methods in which all check information is read out at the end of the circuit. We consider two strategies under this constraint:\n"
msgstr "Di Bagian 1, kita berfokus pada metode di mana seluruh informasi check dibaca di akhir circuit. Kita mempertimbangkan dua strategi di bawah batasan ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetry post-selection: the simplest but most limited form ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)). The check is a rule applied to the measured bitstring, and the original circuit is run unchanged, with no extra qubits, and no encoding. This requires prior knowledge of the ideal output distribution, and the data is consumed by the final measurement before the check is applied.\n"
msgstr "Symmetry post-selection: bentuk paling sederhana tetapi paling terbatas ([Bagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)). Check-nya adalah aturan yang diterapkan pada bitstring hasil pengukuran, dan circuit asli dijalankan tanpa perubahan, tanpa qubit tambahan, dan tanpa encoding. Ini memerlukan pengetahuan awal tentang distribusi output ideal, dan datanya sudah terpakai oleh pengukuran akhir sebelum check diterapkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stabilizer-code post-selection with syndrome qubits ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). The check is the outcome of an ancilla measurement appended to the circuit. This adds qubits and gates, but does not require knowing the full output distribution and can detect both bit-flip and phase-flip Pauli errors.\n"
msgstr "Stabilizer-code post-selection dengan syndrome qubit ([Bagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Check-nya adalah hasil pengukuran ancilla yang ditambahkan ke circuit. Ini menambah qubit dan gate, tetapi tidak memerlukan pengetahuan tentang seluruh distribusi output dan dapat mendeteksi error Pauli bit-flip maupun phase-flip.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both strategies are post-selected: a flagged shot is discarded, and no correction is attempted. [Section 1.3](#limitations) outlines three limitations of end-of-circuit detection that motivate the interior-check constructions of Part 2.\n"
msgstr "Kedua strategi bersifat post-selected: shot yang ditandai dibuang, dan tidak ada upaya koreksi. [Bagian 1.3](#limitations) menguraikan tiga keterbatasan deteksi di akhir circuit yang mendorong konstruksi check interior pada Bagian 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Prerequisite\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Prasyarat\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This part assumes the stabilizer formalism at the level of the IBM Quantum Learning *Foundations of Quantum Error Correction* course, specifically [*Repetition code revisited*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited) and [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes). Codespace, stabilizer generators, syndromes via anti-commutation, code distance, and $[[n,k,d]]$ notation are defined there. We include a short refresher before using these terms operationally in [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"<span id=\"symmetry-post-selection\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini mengasumsikan formalisme stabilizer pada tingkat kursus *Foundations of Quantum Error Correction* di IBM Quantum Learning, khususnya [*Repetition code revisited*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited) dan [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes). Codespace, stabilizer generator, syndrome melalui anti-komutasi, code distance, dan notasi $[[n,k,d]]$ didefinisikan di sana. Kami menyertakan penyegaran singkat sebelum menggunakan istilah-istilah ini secara operasional di [Bagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"<span id=\"symmetry-post-selection\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 Symmetry post-selection on classical bitstrings {#11-symmetry-post-selection-on-classical-bitstrings}"
msgstr "1.1 Symmetry post-selection pada bitstring klasik {#11-symmetry-post-selection-on-classical-bitstrings}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parity checking is a classical error-detection technique. The [parity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_bit) of a bitstring is the number of `1`s it contains, modulo 2. In the example below, a sender appends a parity bit to each data block so that the total number of `1`s in the resulting codeword is even.\n"
msgstr "Check paritas adalah teknik deteksi error klasik. [Paritas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parity_bit) dari sebuah bitstring adalah jumlah `1` di dalamnya, modulo 2. Pada contoh di bawah, pengirim menambahkan sebuah bit paritas ke setiap blok data sehingga total `1` pada codeword yang dihasilkan menjadi genap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Data (7 bits) | Number of 1s | Parity bit | Codeword with even parity (8 bits) |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| `0000000` | 0 | 0 | `00000000` |\n"
"| `1010001` | 3 | 1 | `10100011` |\n"
"| `1101001` | 4 | 0 | `11010010` |\n"
"| `1111111` | 7 | 1 | `11111111` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Data (7 bit) | Jumlah 1 | Bit paritas | Codeword dengan paritas genap (8 bit) |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| `0000000` | 0 | 0 | `00000000` |\n"
"| `1010001` | 3 | 1 | `10100011` |\n"
"| `1101001` | 4 | 0 | `11010010` |\n"
"| `1111111` | 7 | 1 | `11111111` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The receiver recomputes the parity of the 8-bit codeword and rejects it if the parity is no longer even. A single bit-flip during transmission changes the parity by one and is flagged; two flips leave the parity unchanged and slip through undetected.\n"
msgstr "Penerima menghitung ulang paritas dari codeword 8 bit dan menolaknya jika paritasnya tidak lagi genap. Satu bit-flip saat transmisi mengubah paritas sebanyak satu dan akan terdeteksi; dua flip membuat paritas tidak berubah sehingga lolos tanpa terdeteksi.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same idea, a structural rule on the bitstring that valid messages must satisfy, applies to the measurement outcomes of a quantum circuit. Parity is one such rule, but it is not the only one. More generally, when the ideal output distribution of a circuit is restricted by some structural constraint, that constraint can be used as the check: any measured bitstring that violates it can be rejected in classical post-processing as likely corrupted.\n"
msgstr "Ide yang sama, yaitu aturan struktural pada bitstring yang harus dipenuhi oleh pesan yang valid, berlaku juga untuk hasil pengukuran sebuah Circuit kuantum. Paritas adalah salah satu aturan semacam itu, tetapi bukan satu-satunya. Secara lebih umum, ketika distribusi output ideal sebuah Circuit dibatasi oleh suatu batasan struktural, batasan itu bisa dipakai sebagai check: setiap bitstring hasil pengukuran yang melanggarnya bisa ditolak dalam post-processing klasik karena kemungkinan besar rusak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Such constraints typically originate from a [*symmetry*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetry_in_quantum_mechanics) of the ideal state; in other words, an operator $S$ that leaves the state invariant ($S|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$), so that measurement outcomes must respect the constraint associated with $S$. For example, the GHZ state $(|0^n\\rangle + |1^n\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ is stabilized by the pairwise parity operators $Z_i Z_j$, which enforce the all-agree computational-basis support $\\{0^n, 1^n\\}$; it is also stabilized by $X^{\\otimes n}$, which fixes the relative $+$ phase between the two components. As another example, in an occupation-number encoding of an electronic-structure problem, particle-number conservation restricts measurement outcomes to a fixed sector, so outcomes outside that sector can be rejected in classical post-processing as unphysical. This is why the technique is commonly called *symmetry post-selection*. It requires no extra qubits, no encoding, and no syndrome extraction, and thus the original circuit is run unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Batasan semacam ini biasanya berasal dari sebuah [*simetri*](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symmetry_in_quantum_mechanics) dari state ideal; dengan kata lain, sebuah operator $S$ yang membuat state tetap invarian ($S|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$), sehingga hasil pengukuran harus memenuhi batasan yang terkait dengan $S$. Misalnya, state GHZ $(|0^n\\rangle + |1^n\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}$ distabilkan oleh operator paritas berpasangan $Z_i Z_j$, yang memaksa dukungan basis komputasi all-agree $\\{0^n, 1^n\\}$; state ini juga distabilkan oleh $X^{\\otimes n}$, yang mengunci fase relatif $+$ antara kedua komponennya. Contoh lain, pada pengodean occupation-number untuk masalah struktur elektronik, kekekalan jumlah partikel membatasi hasil pengukuran ke sektor tertentu, sehingga hasil di luar sektor itu bisa ditolak dalam post-processing klasik sebagai tidak fisik. Inilah sebabnya teknik ini biasa disebut *symmetry post-selection*. Teknik ini tidak butuh qubit tambahan, tidak butuh pengodean, dan tidak butuh ekstraksi syndrome, sehingga Circuit aslinya dijalankan tanpa perubahan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simplicity comes with two costs. First, the check operates entirely on the post-measurement record: errors that are visible in the bitstring can be flagged, but the quantum information itself is consumed by the final measurement before any check is applied, so the technique cannot protect a state for further use. Second, it requires that the ideal output distribution have a known structure that can be tested directly on a bitstring; for example, the two-bitstring support of a GHZ state, or a fixed particle-number sector of a chemistry ansatz. Most deep computational circuits do not come with such diagnostic structure, in which case no symmetry rule is available. The technique is best viewed as a low-overhead first line of defense for circuits whose ideal output is well understood, rather than a general-purpose detection method.\n"
msgstr "Kesederhanaan ini punya dua harga. Pertama, check bekerja sepenuhnya pada rekaman pasca-pengukuran: error yang terlihat di bitstring bisa ditandai, tetapi informasi kuantumnya sendiri sudah habis terpakai oleh pengukuran akhir sebelum check dilakukan, sehingga teknik ini tidak bisa melindungi state untuk dipakai lebih lanjut. Kedua, teknik ini mensyaratkan distribusi output ideal punya struktur yang dikenal dan bisa diuji langsung pada sebuah bitstring; misalnya dukungan dua-bitstring dari state GHZ, atau sektor jumlah partikel tetap dari ansatz kimia. Sebagian besar Circuit komputasi yang dalam tidak punya struktur diagnostik seperti itu, dan dalam kasus itu tidak ada aturan simetri yang tersedia. Teknik ini paling tepat dipandang sebagai layer pertahanan pertama berbiaya rendah untuk Circuit yang output idealnya dipahami dengan baik, bukan sebagai metode deteksi serbaguna.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even so, symmetry post-selection is an instructive entry point: it is simple enough to expose the core trade-offs of post-selected detection (post-selection rate, sampling overhead, and fidelity) that recur throughout the rest of the notebook. We define these quantities next.\n"
msgstr "Meski begitu, symmetry post-selection adalah pintu masuk yang instruktif: cukup sederhana untuk memperlihatkan trade-off inti dari deteksi dengan post-selection (post-selection rate, sampling overhead, dan fidelity) yang muncul berulang di sisa notebook ini. Kita definisikan besaran-besaran ini berikutnya.\n"

