# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the plot to compare the Hellinger fidelity and acceptance of the two filters. The all-agree rule keeps a subset of the even-parity shots, so its acceptance cannot be higher. This is the accuracy-throughput trade-off introduced by post-selection: stricter filters can make the accepted distribution cleaner, but they also reduce the number of usable samples and therefore raise the sampling overhead. Here both filters preserve the full ideal GHZ support, so Hellinger fidelity cannot decrease as the accepted set shrinks, provided some shots remain. Every shot the all-agree rule keeps lies in the ideal support by construction, so its Hellinger fidelity falls short of 1 only when $0^n$ and $1^n$ are not equally frequent. This distribution-level improvement does not certify phase coherence.\n"
msgstr "Pakai plot untuk membandingkan Hellinger fidelity dan acceptance dari kedua filter. Aturan all-agree menyimpan himpunan bagian dari shot paritas genap, sehingga acceptance-nya tidak mungkin lebih tinggi. Inilah trade-off akurasi-throughput yang diperkenalkan oleh post-selection: filter yang lebih ketat bisa membuat distribusi yang diterima lebih bersih, tetapi juga mengurangi jumlah sampel yang bisa dipakai sehingga menaikkan sampling overhead. Di sini kedua filter mempertahankan seluruh dukungan GHZ ideal, jadi Hellinger fidelity tidak mungkin turun saat himpunan yang diterima menyusut, selama masih ada shot yang tersisa. Setiap shot yang disimpan aturan all-agree berada dalam dukungan ideal menurut konstruksinya, jadi Hellinger fidelity-nya kurang dari 1 hanya ketika $0^n$ dan $1^n$ tidak sama sering muncul. Peningkatan tingkat distribusi ini tidak menjamin koherensi fase.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even parity is good at catching any odd number of bit flips, but it has a structural flaw: any pair of compensating flips slips through. The next subsection addresses this issue.\n"
"<span id=\"parity\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""
"Paritas genap bagus dalam menangkap bit flip berjumlah ganjil, tetapi punya cacat struktural: setiap pasangan flip yang saling mengimbangi akan lolos. Subbagian berikutnya membahas masalah ini.\n"
"<span id=\"parity\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1.2 When parity is not enough {#112-when-parity-is-not-enough}"
msgstr "1.1.2 Ketika paritas tidak cukup {#112-when-parity-is-not-enough}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even parity catches any odd number of bit flips but lets through any even number of flips. We can quantify this directly from the hardware run above: every shot that satisfies the even-parity rule but is *not* in the all-agree set $\\{0^{10}, 1^{10}\\}$ is a corrupted shot that an even number of bit flips moved into the same parity sector as the ideal output.\n"
msgstr "Paritas genap menangkap bit flip berjumlah ganjil tetapi meloloskan flip berjumlah genap. Kita bisa mengukurnya langsung dari eksekusi hardware di atas: setiap shot yang memenuhi aturan paritas genap tetapi *tidak* ada di himpunan all-agree $\\{0^{10}, 1^{10}\\}$ adalah shot rusak yang dipindahkan oleh bit flip berjumlah genap ke sektor paritas yang sama dengan output ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The false-accept rate measures how often the even-parity rule accepts an output outside the ideal support.\n"
msgstr "False-accept rate mengukur seberapa sering aturan paritas genap menerima output di luar dukungan ideal.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous analysis exposes a more fundamental limitation: a final computational-basis filter only sees what is recorded in the bit values. Errors that change bit values (bit-flip errors) leave a trace there and can in principle be filtered. Errors that change only the *phase* between basis states (phase-flip errors) can rotate the relative phase between, say, $|0^n\\rangle$ and $|1^n\\rangle$ without changing the bitstring distribution, so no rule applied only to the final bitstrings can detect them.\n"
msgstr "Analisis sebelumnya memperlihatkan keterbatasan yang lebih mendasar: filter basis komputasi akhir hanya melihat apa yang tercatat di nilai bit. Error yang mengubah nilai bit (error bit-flip) meninggalkan jejak di sana dan pada prinsipnya bisa difilter. Error yang hanya mengubah *fase* antar state basis (error phase-flip) bisa memutar fase relatif antara, misalnya, $|0^n\\rangle$ dan $|1^n\\rangle$ tanpa mengubah distribusi bitstring, sehingga tidak ada aturan yang hanya diterapkan pada bitstring akhir yang bisa mendeteksinya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This limitation motivates the next section. To detect phase-flip errors, the check itself must access information that is not visible in the bitstring, which is what stabilizer codes provide.\n"
msgstr "Keterbatasan ini memotivasi bagian berikutnya. Untuk mendeteksi error phase-flip, check itu sendiri harus mengakses informasi yang tidak terlihat di bitstring, dan itulah yang disediakan oleh stabilizer code.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
