msgstr "Uji pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose you prepare a three-qubit state whose ideal outcomes are only `000` and `111`. What rule would you use for post-selection, and what single-qubit errors would that rule catch?\n"
msgstr "Misalkan kamu menyiapkan state tiga-qubit yang hasil idealnya hanya `000` dan `111`. Aturan apa yang akan kamu pakai untuk post-selection, dan error single-qubit apa yang akan tertangkap oleh aturan itu?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawaban\">\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The natural choice is the *all-agree rule*: keep only `000` and `111`. The even-parity rule does not work here, because `000` has zero $1$s and `111` has three, so their parities are opposite. Any single bit-flip ($X$) error breaks the all-agree pattern, so the rule catches every weight-$1$ bit-flip. It does *not* catch phase-flip ($Z$) errors, which leave bit values unchanged. The phase-flip problem motivates [Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"
msgstr "Pilihan yang wajar adalah *aturan all-agree*: simpan hanya `000` dan `111`. Aturan paritas genap tidak cocok di sini, karena `000` punya nol $1$ dan `111` punya tiga, sehingga paritasnya berlawanan. Setiap error bit-flip ($X$) tunggal merusak pola all-agree, jadi aturan ini menangkap semua bit-flip berbobot-$1$. Aturan ini *tidak* menangkap error phase-flip ($Z$), yang membiarkan nilai bit tidak berubah. Masalah phase-flip inilah yang memotivasi [Bagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"<span id=\"stabilizer-code\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 Stabilizer-code post-selection: the $[[4,2,2]]$ code {#12-stabilizer-code-post-selection-the-422-code}"
msgstr "1.2 Post-selection stabilizer-code: kode $[[4,2,2]]$ {#12-stabilizer-code-post-selection-the-422-code}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) left two open limitations. First, the bitstring rules used there only see what is recorded in the [computational basis](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/quantum-information#measurements-of-quantum-states), that is, the eigenbasis of the $Z$ operator. They cannot see phase-flip errors, which are invisible in that basis. (Changing the measurement basis can make different error information visible, but no single final measurement basis gives a complete, non-destructive check of both bit- and phase-type errors for an arbitrary encoded state.) Second, applying the check requires measuring the data qubits, which collapses the state and consumes the information we wanted to keep. The classical fix to the second problem, keeping redundant copies and checking that they agree, is unavailable here because the [no-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) forbids duplicating an unknown quantum state.\n"
msgstr "[Bagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection) menyisakan dua keterbatasan. Pertama, aturan bitstring yang dipakai di sana hanya melihat apa yang tercatat di [basis komputasi](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/multiple-systems/quantum-information#measurements-of-quantum-states), yaitu eigenbasis dari operator $Z$. Aturan itu tidak bisa melihat error phase-flip, yang tidak terlihat di basis tersebut. (Mengubah basis pengukuran bisa membuat informasi error yang berbeda terlihat, tetapi tidak ada satu basis pengukuran akhir pun yang memberi check lengkap dan non-destruktif untuk error tipe bit maupun fase pada state terenkode sembarang.) Kedua, menerapkan check butuh pengukuran qubit data, yang meruntuhkan state dan menghabiskan informasi yang ingin kita pertahankan. Solusi klasik untuk masalah kedua, yaitu menyimpan salinan redundan dan memeriksa apakah semuanya sama, tidak tersedia di sini karena [no-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) melarang menduplikasi state kuantum yang tidak diketahui.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Why no-cloning matters here\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mengapa no-cloning penting di sini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [no-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) says there is no unitary $U$ that takes an arbitrary unknown state $|\\psi\\rangle$ together with a fresh register and produces $|\\psi\\rangle \\otimes |\\psi\\rangle$. Cloning is a *non-linear* operation in $|\\psi\\rangle$, but every quantum operation is linear: if $U$ cloned the two basis states $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, linearity would force $U$ to send the superposition $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ to $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|1\\rangle)$, which is *not* the cloned state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$. The contradiction arises specifically because the input is a superposition; cloning basis states alone is fine.\n"
msgstr "[No-cloning theorem](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/limitations-on-quantum-information#no-cloning-theorem) menyatakan bahwa tidak ada unitary $U$ yang mengambil state sembarang yang tidak diketahui $|\\psi\\rangle$ bersama register baru lalu menghasilkan $|\\psi\\rangle \\otimes |\\psi\\rangle$. Cloning adalah operasi *non-linear* terhadap $|\\psi\\rangle$, padahal setiap operasi kuantum bersifat linear: jika $U$ meng-clone dua state basis $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$, maka linearitas akan memaksa $U$ mengubah superposisi $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$ menjadi $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle|1\\rangle)$, yang *bukan* state hasil clone $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle) \\otimes \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)$. Kontradiksi ini muncul tepat karena inputnya berupa superposisi; meng-clone state basis saja tidak masalah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This does not forbid preparing multiple copies of a state we *already know how to prepare*: we can simply run the preparation procedure on fresh registers. A CNOT cleanly copies computational-basis information, sending $|a\\rangle|0\\rangle \\mapsto |a\\rangle|a\\rangle$ for $a \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, but this does not extend to arbitrary superpositions. The encoding circuits used by stabilizer codes combine the logical input, which may be unknown, with initialized ancillas and distribute its information across an encoded register without making copies. What no-cloning rules out is duplicating a state that arrives unknown from an earlier computation.\n"
msgstr "Ini tidak melarang pembuatan banyak salinan dari state yang *sudah kita ketahui cara menyiapkannya*: kita cukup menjalankan prosedur persiapan pada register baru. Sebuah CNOT menyalin informasi basis komputasi dengan bersih, mengubah $|a\\rangle|0\\rangle \\mapsto |a\\rangle|a\\rangle$ untuk $a \\in \\{0, 1\\}$, tetapi ini tidak meluas ke superposisi sembarang. Circuit pengodean yang dipakai stabilizer code menggabungkan input logis, yang bisa jadi tidak diketahui, dengan ancilla yang diinisialisasi dan menyebarkan informasinya ke seluruh register terenkode tanpa membuat salinan. Yang dilarang oleh no-cloning adalah menduplikasi state yang datang tanpa diketahui dari komputasi sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Stabilizer codes resolve both limitations at once. The [logical state](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited#syndromes) is encoded across multiple physical qubits through entanglement, and an ancilla qubit couples to the data to report a stabilizer eigenvalue, enough to flag whether the state has left the [codespace](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes), but not enough to reveal the logical amplitudes. By using two complementary stabilizers, one diagonal in the $Z$ basis and one in the $X$ basis, the check is sensitive to both bit-flip and phase-flip errors. Because only the ancilla is measured, this can in principle be applied without collapsing the encoded state. Used this way, the code is post-selected quantum error correction in its original form: an error-detecting code whose flagged shots are discarded rather than corrected. The reach of the check is bounded by the *code distance* $d$: with $d=2$, the $[[4,2,2]]$ code we use here detects every weight-$1$ Pauli error on a data qubit but is blind to certain weight-$2$ errors, including the even-bit-flip patterns that already escaped the parity rule in [Section 1.1.2](#parity).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Stabilizer code menyelesaikan kedua keterbatasan sekaligus. [State logis](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/repetition-code-revisited#syndromes) dienkode ke beberapa qubit fisik melalui entanglement, dan sebuah qubit ancilla terkopel ke data untuk melaporkan eigenvalue stabilizer, cukup untuk menandai apakah state sudah keluar dari [codespace](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes), tetapi tidak cukup untuk mengungkap amplitudo logisnya. Dengan memakai dua stabilizer yang saling komplementer, satu diagonal di basis $Z$ dan satu di basis $X$, check ini peka terhadap error bit-flip maupun phase-flip. Karena hanya ancilla yang diukur, ini pada prinsipnya bisa diterapkan tanpa meruntuhkan state terenkode. Dipakai dengan cara ini, kode tersebut adalah koreksi error kuantum dengan post-selection dalam bentuk aslinya: kode pendeteksi error yang shot-nya, jika ditandai, dibuang alih-alih dikoreksi. Jangkauan check dibatasi oleh *code distance* $d$: dengan $d=2$, kode $[[4,2,2]]$ yang kita pakai di sini mendeteksi setiap error Pauli berbobot-$1$ pada qubit data tetapi buta terhadap error berbobot-$2$ tertentu, termasuk pola bit-flip genap yang sebelumnya sudah lolos dari aturan paritas di [Bagian 1.1.2](#parity).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Quick refresher on stabilizer-code terminology\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penyegaran singkat tentang terminologi stabilizer-code\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms collected below are the ones used most often in this section. For full details, refer to the IBM Quantum Learning [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes) course.\n"
msgstr "Istilah-istilah yang terkumpul di bawah adalah yang paling sering dipakai di bagian ini. Untuk detail lengkap, lihat kursus IBM Quantum Learning [*Stabilizer codes*](/learning/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-correction/stabilizer-formalism/stabilizer-codes).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Physical qubit, logical qubit.* The hardware qubits used to store encoded information are the physical qubits. The abstract qubits whose state is being protected are the logical qubits.\n"
msgstr "*Qubit fisik, qubit logis.* Qubit hardware yang dipakai untuk menyimpan informasi terenkode adalah qubit fisik. Qubit abstrak yang state-nya sedang dilindungi adalah qubit logis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Stabilizer generators.* A set of mutually commuting multi-qubit Pauli operators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$. The states satisfying $P_k|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$ for every $k$ form the codespace.\n"
msgstr "*Stabilizer generator.* Himpunan operator Pauli multi-qubit yang saling komutatif $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$. State yang memenuhi $P_k|\\psi\\rangle = |\\psi\\rangle$ untuk setiap $k$ membentuk codespace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Codespace.* The simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of the stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr "*Codespace.* Eigenspace $+1$ simultan dari stabilizer generator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Ancilla qubit.* An auxiliary qubit coupled to the data qubits to extract a stabilizer eigenvalue without measuring the data directly.\n"
msgstr "*Qubit ancilla.* Qubit tambahan yang terkopel ke qubit data untuk mengekstrak eigenvalue stabilizer tanpa mengukur data secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Syndrome.* The string of stabilizer-measurement outcomes, under the convention that outcome `0` corresponds to eigenvalue $+1$ and outcome `1` to eigenvalue $-1$.\n"
msgstr "*Syndrome.* String hasil pengukuran stabilizer, dengan konvensi bahwa hasil `0` sesuai dengan eigenvalue $+1$ dan hasil `1` dengan eigenvalue $-1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*$[[n, k, d]]$ notation.* A stabilizer code on $n$ physical qubits that encodes $k$ logical qubits with code distance $d$.\n"
msgstr "*Notasi $[[n, k, d]]$.* Stabilizer code pada $n$ qubit fisik yang mengenkode $k$ qubit logis dengan code distance $d$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Weight of a Pauli operator.* The number of qubits on which the operator acts as something other than the identity.\n"
msgstr "*Bobot operator Pauli.* Jumlah qubit tempat operator bekerja sebagai sesuatu selain identitas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Logical operator.* A Pauli operator that commutes with every stabilizer generator and is not proportional to a stabilizer element.\n"
msgstr "*Operator logis.* Operator Pauli yang komutatif dengan setiap stabilizer generator dan tidak proporsional dengan elemen stabilizer.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Code distance $d$.* The minimum weight of a logical operator.\n"
msgstr "*Code distance $d$.* Bobot minimum dari sebuah operator logis.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"The $[[4,2,2]]$ code uses $n=4$ physical qubits to encode $k=2$ logical qubits with code distance $d=2$. Its codespace is the simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of two stabilizer generators,\n"
"$$\n"
"Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0.\n"
"$$\n"
"A single-qubit $X$ error anti-commutes with $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and is flagged by the corresponding syndrome bit; a single-qubit $Z$ error anti-commutes with $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ and is flagged by the other. Every weight-$1$ Pauli error on a data qubit is detected by at least one of the two stabilizers. The two-bit syndrome identifies the error type ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, or none) but not the qubit on which the error occurred. With $d=2$, this information is insufficient to determine a correction, so the $[[4,2,2]]$ code is used as a detection-only code.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Kode $[[4,2,2]]$ memakai $n=4$ qubit fisik untuk mengenkode $k=2$ qubit logis dengan code distance $d=2$. Codespace-nya adalah eigenspace $+1$ simultan dari dua stabilizer generator,\n"
"$$\n"
"Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0.\n"
"$$\n"
"Error $X$ single-qubit anti-komutatif dengan $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan ditandai oleh bit syndrome yang bersesuaian; error $Z$ single-qubit anti-komutatif dengan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ dan ditandai oleh bit yang lain. Setiap error Pauli berbobot-$1$ pada qubit data terdeteksi oleh setidaknya satu dari dua stabilizer. Syndrome dua-bit mengidentifikasi jenis error ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, atau tidak ada) tetapi bukan qubit tempat error terjadi. Dengan $d=2$, informasi ini tidak cukup untuk menentukan koreksi, sehingga kode $[[4,2,2]]$ dipakai sebagai kode yang hanya mendeteksi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The experiments below run syndrome extraction on the logical Bell state:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"a state in the codespace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen di bawah menjalankan ekstraksi syndrome pada state Bell logis:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"sebuah state di dalam codespace.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Logical basis states of the [[4,2,2]] code\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"State basis logis dari kode [[4,2,2]]\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The $[[4,2,2]]$ code encodes two logical qubits using four physical qubits. As with any two-qubit system, there are four logical computational-basis states, $|00\\rangle_L$, $|01\\rangle_L$, $|10\\rangle_L$, $|11\\rangle_L$, read as the values of the two encoded qubits (for example, $|00\\rangle_L$ has both logical qubits in the logical-zero state). What makes this an *encoding* is that each $|ab\\rangle_L$ is a specific superposition of physical four-qubit basis states, chosen so that all four logical basis states satisfy the codespace conditions $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 = +1$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0 = +1$.\n"
msgstr "Kode $[[4,2,2]]$ mengenkode dua qubit logis memakai empat qubit fisik. Seperti sistem dua-qubit mana pun, ada empat state basis komputasi logis, $|00\\rangle_L$, $|01\\rangle_L$, $|10\\rangle_L$, $|11\\rangle_L$, yang dibaca sebagai nilai dua qubit terenkode (misalnya, $|00\\rangle_L$ memiliki kedua qubit logis dalam state logical-zero). Yang membuat ini sebuah *pengodean* adalah bahwa setiap $|ab\\rangle_L$ merupakan superposisi spesifik dari state basis empat-qubit fisik, yang dipilih sehingga keempat state basis logis memenuhi kondisi codespace $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0 = +1$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0 = +1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The standard choice is\n"
msgstr "Pilihan standarnya adalah\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|00\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|01\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0011\\rangle + |1100\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|10\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0101\\rangle + |1010\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|11\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|00\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|01\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0011\\rangle + |1100\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|10\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0101\\rangle + |1010\\rangle\\big), \\\\\n"
"|11\\rangle_L &= \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each line pairs two four-qubit strings related by flipping all four bits. Both strings in each line have an even number of $1$s. Since $Z$ has eigenvalue $+1$ on $|0\\rangle$ and $-1$ on $|1\\rangle$, the eigenvalue of $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ on a computational-basis string is $(-1)^{\\text{number of }1\\text{s}}$, so a string with an even number of $1$s gives eigenvalue $+1$. The $+$ combination is also invariant under $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, which simply permutes the two terms within each line.\n"
msgstr "Setiap baris memasangkan dua string empat-qubit yang terkait lewat pembalikan keempat bit. Kedua string di setiap baris memiliki jumlah $1$ yang genap. Karena $Z$ memiliki eigenvalue $+1$ pada $|0\\rangle$ dan $-1$ pada $|1\\rangle$, eigenvalue $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ pada string basis komputasi adalah $(-1)^{\\text{jumlah }1\\text{ }}$, sehingga string dengan jumlah $1$ genap memberi eigenvalue $+1$. Kombinasi $+$ juga invarian terhadap $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, yang hanya menukar dua suku dalam setiap baris.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logical Bell state used in the experiments is:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"the analog of the standard Bell state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ on the two logical qubits. Substituting the codeword expressions above gives its physical four-qubit form:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle + |0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"State Bell logis yang dipakai dalam eksperimen adalah:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}\\big(|00\\rangle_L + |11\\rangle_L\\big),\n"
"$$\n"
"analog dari state Bell standar $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ pada dua qubit logis. Dengan mensubstitusi ekspresi codeword di atas, kita dapatkan bentuk empat-qubit fisiknya:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L = \\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|0000\\rangle + |1111\\rangle + |0110\\rangle + |1001\\rangle\\big).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The preparation circuit applies two H + CNOT pairs, on $(q_0, q_3)$ and $(q_1, q_2)$. Each pair produces a physical Bell state $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ on its two qubits, so the full four-qubit output is the tensor product:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_0 q_3} \\otimes \\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_1 q_2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Expanding this tensor product, the four computational-basis strings that appear with equal amplitude are $|0000\\rangle, |1111\\rangle, |0110\\rangle, |1001\\rangle$, the same four strings that appear in the expression for $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ above. The circuit therefore prepares $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ directly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Circuit persiapan menerapkan dua pasangan H + CNOT, pada $(q_0, q_3)$ dan $(q_1, q_2)$. Setiap pasangan menghasilkan state Bell fisik $\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt 2}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ pada dua qubitnya, sehingga output empat-qubit penuhnya adalah hasil kali tensor:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\tfrac{1}{2}\\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_0 q_3} \\otimes \\big(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle\\big)_{q_1 q_2}.\n"
"$$\n"
"Setelah hasil kali tensor ini diperluas, empat string basis komputasi yang muncul dengan amplitudo sama adalah $|0000\\rangle, |1111\\rangle, |0110\\rangle, |1001\\rangle$, empat string yang sama dengan yang muncul dalam ekspresi untuk $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ di atas. Jadi Circuit ini langsung menyiapkan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We start by building the circuit that prepares the logical Bell state $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. The construction uses two H + CNOT pairs to create two physical Bell pairs: one between data qubits 0 and 3, the other between data qubits 1 and 2. Their tensor product lies inside the $[[4,2,2]]$ codespace and is equal to $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ as defined in the previous section.\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan membangun Circuit yang menyiapkan state Bell logis $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$. Konstruksinya memakai dua pasangan H + CNOT untuk membuat dua pasangan Bell fisik: satu antara qubit data 0 dan 3, satunya lagi antara qubit data 1 dan 2. Hasil kali tensornya berada di dalam codespace $[[4,2,2]]$ dan sama dengan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ seperti didefinisikan di bagian sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/850496ab-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/850496ab-0.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we extract both syndromes simultaneously. The $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ check is implemented by applying CNOTs from each data qubit into a single ancilla, so the ancilla parity records the joint $Z$-eigenvalue. The $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ check uses Hadamard conjugation: applying H gates on the data qubits before and after the CNOTs converts the $X$-parity check into a $Z$-parity check on a rotated frame, which the same CNOT pattern then extracts onto a second ancilla.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita ekstrak kedua syndrome secara bersamaan. Check $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ diimplementasikan dengan menerapkan CNOT dari setiap qubit data ke satu ancilla, sehingga paritas ancilla merekam eigenvalue $Z$ gabungan. Check $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ memakai konjugasi Hadamard: menerapkan Gate H pada qubit data sebelum dan sesudah CNOT mengubah check paritas-$X$ menjadi check paritas-$Z$ pada kerangka yang diputar, yang kemudian diekstrak oleh pola CNOT yang sama ke ancilla kedua.\n"

