msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/0dda3dbd-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2.1 Simulator validation {#121-simulator-validation}"
msgstr "1.2.1 Validasi simulator {#121-simulator-validation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before running on hardware, we verify the syndrome extraction on a noiseless simulator. We prepare the logical Bell state $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ and measure both stabilizers, $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, onto separate ancillas. Since $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ lies in the codespace, both syndrome bits should return `0` deterministically.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum menjalankan di hardware, kita verifikasi ekstraksi syndrome pada simulator tanpa noise. Kita siapkan state Bell logis $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ dan ukur kedua stabilizer, $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, ke ancilla yang terpisah. Karena $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ berada di codespace, kedua bit syndrome seharusnya mengembalikan `0` secara deterministik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both syndrome bits return `0` deterministically on the clean logical Bell state, confirming that $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ lies in the simultaneous $+1$ eigenspace of $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ and $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, that is, in the codespace.\n"
msgstr "Kedua bit syndrome mengembalikan `0` secara deterministik pada state Bell logis yang bersih, yang mengonfirmasi bahwa $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ berada di eigenspace $+1$ simultan dari $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ dan $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$, yaitu di dalam codespace.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before moving to hardware, we walk through how the two stabilizers respond to single-qubit Pauli errors. A stabilizer measurement returns $-1$ (syndrome bit `1`) when the error operator anti-commutes with the stabilizer, and $+1$ (syndrome bit `0`) when it commutes. This follows from how Pauli operators act on eigenstates: if $S|\\psi\\rangle = +|\\psi\\rangle$ and $E$ anti-commutes with $S$ ($ES = -SE$), then $S(E|\\psi\\rangle) = -E S|\\psi\\rangle = -E|\\psi\\rangle$, so the corrupted state $E|\\psi\\rangle$ is a $-1$ eigenstate of $S$.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum pindah ke hardware, kita telusuri bagaimana kedua stabilizer merespons error Pauli single-qubit. Pengukuran stabilizer mengembalikan $-1$ (bit syndrome `1`) ketika operator error anti-komutatif dengan stabilizer, dan $+1$ (bit syndrome `0`) ketika komutatif. Ini mengikuti cara operator Pauli bekerja pada eigenstate: jika $S|\\psi\\rangle = +|\\psi\\rangle$ dan $E$ anti-komutatif dengan $S$ ($ES = -SE$), maka $S(E|\\psi\\rangle) = -E S|\\psi\\rangle = -E|\\psi\\rangle$, sehingga state yang rusak $E|\\psi\\rangle$ adalah eigenstate $-1$ dari $S$.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We verify this directly on the simulator by injecting $X$, $Z$, and $Y$ errors on different data qubits and reading both syndrome bits.\n"
msgstr "Kita verifikasi ini langsung di simulator dengan menyuntikkan error $X$, $Z$, dan $Y$ pada qubit data yang berbeda dan membaca kedua bit syndrome.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulation confirms the anti-commutation analysis: every single-qubit $X$ error gives the same syndrome regardless of which data qubit it hits, and similarly for $Z$ and $Y$. The four possible outcomes of the two-bit syndrome correspond cleanly to four error classes (the table below lists the syndrome bits as $(s_X, s_Z)$, matching the displayed [bitstring order convention in Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) `c[1] c[0]`):\n"
msgstr "Simulasi mengonfirmasi analisis anti-komutasi: setiap error $X$ single-qubit memberi syndrome yang sama tidak peduli qubit data mana yang terkena, begitu pula untuk $Z$ dan $Y$. Empat hasil yang mungkin dari syndrome dua-bit sesuai dengan jelas dengan empat kelas error (tabel di bawah mencantumkan bit syndrome sebagai $(s_X, s_Z)$, sesuai dengan [konvensi urutan bitstring di Qiskit](/guides/bit-ordering) yang ditampilkan `c[1] c[0]`):\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Error on any single data qubit | $s_X$ | $s_Z$ |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| no error | `0` | `0` |\n"
"| $X$ | `0` | `1` |\n"
"| $Z$ | `1` | `0` |\n"
"| $Y$ | `1` | `1` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Error pada satu qubit data mana pun | $s_X$ | $s_Z$ |\n"
"|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n"
"| tidak ada error | `0` | `0` |\n"
"| $X$ | `0` | `1` |\n"
"| $Z$ | `1` | `0` |\n"
"| $Y$ | `1` | `1` |\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two limitations of this scheme are worth stating now. First, the table identifies the *type* of error ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, or none) but not the *qubit* on which the error occurred: an $X$ error on data qubit 0 and an $X$ error on data qubit 2 produce identical syndromes, as the simulation shows directly. Without knowing the qubit location we cannot apply a corresponding inverse to undo the error, which is why we use the $[[4,2,2]]$ code for detection only: we post-select on $s_X = s_Z = 0$ and do not attempt correction. Second, the table covers only single-qubit errors; certain weight-2 errors commute with both stabilizers and escape the syndrome entirely. We return to that limitation in [Section 1.3](#limitations).\n"
msgstr "Dua keterbatasan skema ini perlu disebutkan sekarang. Pertama, tabel mengidentifikasi *jenis* error ($X$, $Z$, $Y$, atau tidak ada) tetapi bukan *qubit* tempat error terjadi: error $X$ pada qubit data 0 dan error $X$ pada qubit data 2 menghasilkan syndrome yang identik, seperti yang diperlihatkan langsung oleh simulasi. Tanpa mengetahui lokasi qubit, kita tidak bisa menerapkan kebalikan yang sesuai untuk membatalkan error, itulah sebabnya kita memakai kode $[[4,2,2]]$ hanya untuk deteksi: kita melakukan post-select pada $s_X = s_Z = 0$ dan tidak mencoba koreksi. Kedua, tabel hanya mencakup error single-qubit; error berbobot-2 tertentu komutatif dengan kedua stabilizer dan lolos dari syndrome sepenuhnya. Kita kembali ke keterbatasan itu di [Bagian 1.3](#limitations).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Uji pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We just saw that an $X$ error flips the $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$ syndrome, and a $Z$ error would flip the $X_3X_2X_1X_0$ syndrome. What happens if a $Y$ error hits a single data qubit? Which stabilizer or stabilizers would detect it?\n"
msgstr "Kita baru saja melihat bahwa error $X$ membalik syndrome $Z_3Z_2Z_1Z_0$, dan error $Z$ akan membalik syndrome $X_3X_2X_1X_0$. Apa yang terjadi jika error $Y$ mengenai satu qubit data? Stabilizer mana yang akan mendeteksinya?\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Hint:* $Y = iXZ$, so a $Y$ error is both a bit-flip and a phase-flip on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr "*Petunjuk:* $Y = iXZ$, jadi error $Y$ adalah bit-flip sekaligus phase-flip pada qubit yang sama.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since $Y = iXZ$, it anti-commutes with both $Z$-type and $X$-type stabilizer operators on the affected qubit. A single $Y$ error therefore triggers both stabilizers at once, giving syndrome $s_Z = 1$ and $s_X = 1$. The four single-qubit Pauli outcomes (none, $X$, $Z$, $Y$) map to four distinct syndrome patterns, as the simulation above confirms.\n"
msgstr "Karena $Y = iXZ$, ia anti-komutatif dengan operator stabilizer tipe-$Z$ maupun tipe-$X$ pada qubit yang terkena. Jadi satu error $Y$ memicu kedua stabilizer sekaligus, memberi syndrome $s_Z = 1$ dan $s_X = 1$. Keempat hasil Pauli single-qubit (tidak ada, $X$, $Z$, $Y$) dipetakan ke empat pola syndrome yang berbeda, seperti dikonfirmasi oleh simulasi di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2.2 Hardware demonstration: joint $Z$ and $X$ syndrome extraction {#122-hardware-demonstration-joint-z-and-x-syndrome-extraction}"
msgstr "1.2.2 Demonstrasi hardware: ekstraksi syndrome $Z$ dan $X$ gabungan {#122-hardware-demonstration-joint-z-and-x-syndrome-extraction}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now run the same circuit on hardware and quantify the trade-off introduced by post-selecting on $s_X = s_Z = 0$. The metrics we report are the post-selection rate $A$ (fraction of shots that pass both checks), the sampling overhead $1/A$, and the Hellinger fidelity to the ideal data-qubit distribution before and after post-selection.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita jalankan Circuit yang sama di hardware dan mengukur trade-off yang muncul dari post-selection pada $s_X = s_Z = 0$. Metrik yang kita laporkan adalah post-selection rate $A$ (fraksi shot yang lolos kedua check), sampling overhead $1/A$, dan Hellinger fidelity terhadap distribusi qubit data ideal sebelum dan sesudah post-selection.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware circuit reuses the syndrome-extraction circuit `qc_check` built in the simulator validation above and adds measurements on the four data qubits at the end, in keeping with the end-of-circuit detection scope in Part 1. The two registers are kept separate: the syndrome bits land in `c` ($s_Z = c[0]$, $s_X = c[1]$), and the four data bits land in a new register `data_c`.\n"
msgstr "Circuit hardware memakai ulang Circuit ekstraksi syndrome `qc_check` yang dibangun pada validasi simulator di atas dan menambahkan pengukuran pada empat qubit data di akhir, sesuai dengan cakupan deteksi akhir-Circuit di Bagian 1. Kedua register dipisahkan: bit syndrome masuk ke `c` ($s_Z = c[0]$, $s_X = c[1]$), dan empat bit data masuk ke register baru `data_c`.\n"

