# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.3 Limits of end-of-circuit detection {#13-limits-of-end-of-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "1.3 Batasan deteksi di akhir Circuit {#13-limits-of-end-of-circuit-detection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So far we have looked at end-of-circuit post-selection through two examples: bitstring filtering ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) and stabilizer-code post-selection ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Three limitations follow from the architecture they share.\n"
msgstr "Sejauh ini kita sudah melihat post-selection di akhir Circuit lewat dua contoh: pemfilteran bitstring ([Bagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) dan post-selection dengan kode stabilizer ([Bagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code)). Ada tiga batasan yang muncul dari arsitektur yang sama-sama mereka pakai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Some errors are not flagged**\n"
msgstr "**Beberapa error tidak terdeteksi**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With $d = 2$, weight-$2$ Pauli operators that act non-trivially on the encoded data can commute with both stabilizers and therefore go undetected. The reach is set by the code distance: detecting more errors of higher weight requires a code with larger $d$.\n"
msgstr "Dengan $d = 2$, operator Pauli berbobot-$2$ yang bekerja secara non-trivial pada data terenkode bisa komut dengan kedua stabilizer sehingga lolos tanpa terdeteksi. Jangkauannya ditentukan oleh jarak kode: untuk mendeteksi lebih banyak error berbobot lebih tinggi, kita butuh kode dengan $d$ yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The syndrome does not localize the fault**\n"
msgstr "**Syndrome tidak melokalisasi fault**\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When a syndrome bit fires, the syndrome record tells us that something went wrong somewhere in the circuit but not on which qubit, in which gate layer, or whether the underlying fault was a gate error in the payload, a gate error in the syndrome extraction, or a measurement readout error on the data or ancilla qubits. The single-shot ambiguity reported in the false-accept table (multiple ideal codewords often equally close in bitstring distance) is consistent with the same limit.\n"
msgstr "Saat sebuah bit syndrome menyala, catatan syndrome hanya memberi tahu kita bahwa ada yang salah di suatu tempat dalam Circuit, tapi tidak di qubit mana, di layer gate mana, atau apakah fault yang mendasarinya berupa error gate pada payload, error gate pada ekstraksi syndrome, atau error readout pengukuran pada qubit data atau ancilla. Ambiguitas single-shot yang dilaporkan di tabel false-accept (beberapa codeword ideal sering sama dekatnya dalam jarak bitstring) konsisten dengan batasan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Detection itself adds gates**\n"
msgstr "**Deteksi itu sendiri menambah gate**\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the logical level, the $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ preparation uses four gates (two H + two CNOT), and the joint $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ + $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ syndrome extraction adds 16 logical gates (four CNOT for Z-check + 12 gates for X-check with Hadamard conjugation) and two ancilla qubits. However, transpilation to hardware-native gates increases these counts, as the cell below demonstrates.\n"
msgstr "Di tingkat logis, persiapan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ memakai empat gate (dua H + dua CNOT), dan ekstraksi syndrome gabungan $Z_3 Z_2 Z_1 Z_0$ + $X_3 X_2 X_1 X_0$ menambah 16 gate logis (empat CNOT untuk Z-check + 12 gate untuk X-check dengan konjugasi Hadamard) dan dua qubit ancilla. Namun, transpilasi ke gate native hardware menaikkan jumlah ini, seperti yang ditunjukkan sel di bawah.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example is intentionally extreme. In the $[[4,2,2]]$ code, the $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ preparation here uses only four logical gates, so the syndrome-extraction block makes up most of the transpiled circuit. The gate-count comparison above illustrates a large relative overhead. When the payload is minimal, syndrome extraction can dominate the total gate count. In a payload with many more gates, the same fixed-size syndrome block would be a smaller fraction of the total. The conclusion that the syndrome-extraction circuit is itself noisy still holds, even though the ratio above does not.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini sengaja dibuat ekstrem. Pada kode $[[4,2,2]]$, persiapan $|\\Phi^+\\rangle_L$ di sini hanya memakai empat gate logis, jadi blok ekstraksi syndrome menyusun sebagian besar Circuit hasil transpilasi. Perbandingan jumlah gate di atas menggambarkan overhead relatif yang besar. Saat payload minimal, ekstraksi syndrome bisa mendominasi total jumlah gate. Pada payload dengan jauh lebih banyak gate, blok syndrome berukuran tetap yang sama akan jadi porsi yang lebih kecil dari total. Kesimpulan bahwa Circuit ekstraksi syndrome itu sendiri berisik tetap berlaku, meskipun rasio di atas tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cost depends on the code's stabilizer count and weights, routing, and ancilla reuse (note the scaling question above). As target circuits grow toward utility scale (40+ qubits), end-of-circuit code-based detection in this direct form might not be the most efficient option on near-term hardware.\n"
msgstr "Biayanya bergantung pada jumlah dan bobot stabilizer kode, routing, dan pemakaian ulang ancilla (perhatikan pertanyaan penskalaan di atas). Saat Circuit target tumbuh ke skala utility (40+ qubit), deteksi berbasis kode di akhir Circuit dalam bentuk langsung ini mungkin bukan pilihan paling efisien di hardware near-term.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 2: Mid-circuit detection {#part-2-mid-circuit-detection}"
msgstr "Bagian 2: Deteksi di tengah Circuit {#part-2-mid-circuit-detection}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 1.3](#limitations) listed three limitations of end-of-circuit detection: certain weight-2 errors go undetected, the syndrome does not localize the fault, and a fixed syndrome-extraction block is applied to every shot. In Part 2, we move detection inside the circuit and partially address the third limitation. Checks couple ancillas to the data at selected circuit locations, including interior points. In these examples, the ancillas are measured at the end alongside the data, and post-selection happens in classical post-processing. When lighter checks are distributed across multiple interior points, the per-shot gate cost can track the circuit structure rather than a fixed code block. Some faults still pass undetected, and these checks do not in general identify a unique fault location.\n"
msgstr "[Bagian 1.3](#limitations) mendaftar tiga batasan deteksi di akhir Circuit: error berbobot-2 tertentu tidak terdeteksi, syndrome tidak melokalisasi error, dan blok ekstraksi syndrome berukuran tetap diterapkan di setiap shot. Di Bagian 2, kita memindahkan deteksi ke dalam Circuit dan mengatasi sebagian batasan ketiga. Check menghubungkan ancilla ke data di lokasi Circuit tertentu, termasuk titik-titik interior. Dalam contoh ini, ancilla diukur di akhir bersama data, dan post-selection terjadi di post-processing klasik. Saat check yang lebih ringan disebar di beberapa titik interior, biaya gate per shot bisa mengikuti struktur Circuit, bukan blok kode tetap. Sebagian error masih lolos tanpa terdeteksi, dan check ini pada umumnya tidak mengidentifikasi lokasi error yang unik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We work through two ideas:\n"
msgstr "Kita bahas dua gagasan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coherent Pauli checks (Sections [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)): the algebraic foundation. For any Clifford payload $U$ and post-payload check $R$, the pre-payload check $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ defines a valid check pair.\n"
msgstr "Coherent Pauli checks (Bagian [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)): fondasi aljabarnya. Untuk payload Clifford $U$ apa pun dan check pasca-payload $R$, check pra-payload $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ menentukan pasangan check yang valid.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spacetime codes (Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)): a hardware-aware refinement. Place lightweight checks at points in the circuit where the local stabilizer structure makes $L$ unnecessary, and trace their detection regions through the circuit graph.\n"
msgstr "Spacetime code (Bagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)): penyempurnaan yang sadar hardware. Tempatkan check ringan di titik-titik Circuit yang struktur stabilizer lokalnya membuat $L$ tidak diperlukan, lalu telusuri daerah deteksinya lewat graf Circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both CPC and spacetime codes are designed for *Clifford circuits* (or circuits dominated by Clifford gates). The space of valid checks shrinks exponentially as non-Clifford content increases ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, 2025, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). The random Clifford payload used in Part 2 is entirely Clifford, which is why it is a convenient testbed.\n"
msgstr "CPC maupun spacetime code dirancang untuk *Circuit Clifford* (atau Circuit yang didominasi gate Clifford). Ruang check yang valid menyusut secara eksponensial seiring bertambahnya konten non-Clifford ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, 2025, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)). Payload Clifford acak yang dipakai di Bagian 2 sepenuhnya Clifford, itulah sebabnya ia jadi testbed yang praktis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 From end-of-circuit filtering to mid-circuit checks {#21-from-end-of-circuit-filtering-to-mid-circuit-checks}"
msgstr "2.1 Dari pemfilteran di akhir Circuit ke check di tengah Circuit {#21-from-end-of-circuit-filtering-to-mid-circuit-checks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "End-of-circuit post-selection collects all check information from a final measurement. The checks can only see the cumulative effect of errors across the entire circuit. Mid-circuit checks change *what* the detection can see. A check ancilla couples to the data at selected points during the circuit. In these examples it is measured at the end alongside the data, and post-selection rejects flagged shots in classical post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Post-selection di akhir Circuit mengumpulkan seluruh informasi check dari pengukuran akhir. Check hanya bisa melihat efek kumulatif error di seluruh Circuit. Check di tengah Circuit mengubah *apa* yang bisa dilihat deteksi. Sebuah ancilla check terhubung ke data di titik-titik tertentu selama Circuit berjalan. Dalam contoh ini ia diukur di akhir bersama data, dan post-selection menolak shot yang ditandai di post-processing klasik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The framework for mid-circuit checks is *coherent Pauli checks (CPC)*, introduced in [Section 2.2](#coherent). CPC tells us *what* to check and *why* the check is guaranteed to pass on an error-free circuit. The challenge is making these checks practical. A CPC-derived check can involve a high-weight Pauli operator spanning many qubits, which on a connectivity-constrained device requires routing gates that add more noise than the check removes. [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) address this directly. *Spacetime codes* keep the same CPC algebra but constrain checks to be spatially local, spreading their sensitivity across many circuit layers instead of many qubits. This transition begins in Section 2.3.3 and is developed in Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment).\n"
msgstr "Kerangka kerja untuk check di tengah Circuit adalah *coherent Pauli checks (CPC)*, diperkenalkan di [Bagian 2.2](#coherent). CPC memberi tahu kita *apa* yang harus dicek dan *mengapa* check dijamin lolos pada Circuit tanpa error. Tantangannya adalah membuat check ini praktis. Check turunan CPC bisa melibatkan operator Pauli berbobot tinggi yang mencakup banyak qubit, yang pada perangkat dengan konektivitas terbatas membutuhkan gate routing yang menambah lebih banyak noise daripada yang dihilangkan check. [Martiel & Javadi-Abhari (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725) membahas hal ini secara langsung. *Spacetime code* mempertahankan aljabar CPC yang sama tapi membatasi check agar lokal secara spasial, menyebarkan sensitivitasnya ke banyak lapisan Circuit alih-alih banyak qubit. Transisi ini dimulai di Bagian 2.3.3 dan dikembangkan di Bagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"What &quot;mid-circuit&quot; really means in this lesson\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Arti sebenarnya &quot;mid-circuit&quot; dalam pelajaran ini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The benefit of a mid-circuit check is not the timing of the measurement, but the fact that *the check couples to the circuit at an interior point*, which means that its detection region can be tailored to selected parts of the payload. When we say \"mid-circuit check,\" think \"interior-coupled check with a spacetime detection region.\"\n"
msgstr "Manfaat check di tengah Circuit bukan pada waktu pengukurannya, melainkan pada kenyataan bahwa *check terhubung ke Circuit di titik interior*, yang berarti daerah deteksinya bisa disesuaikan untuk bagian payload tertentu. Saat kita bilang \"check di tengah Circuit\", bayangkan \"check yang terhubung di interior dengan daerah deteksi spacetime\".\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) hardware experiment, each check ancilla couples to the payload at a few points along a target wire and is measured at the *end of the circuit* alongside the data qubits, not at an intermediate point with reset and reuse. Its sensitivity nevertheless extends *into the circuit interior* because the check operator propagates through the payload under conjugation (discussed in [Section 2.4](#paulice)). What we demonstrate is the spacetime-code principle, checks whose detection regions extend deep into the circuit's interior, even though the measurement happens at the boundary. A fully mid-circuit implementation (measure, reset, reuse) would further reduce idle time on ancillas and is an important engineering step. See [Lanes et al. (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.20658) for how dynamic circuit capabilities enable these protocols at scale.\n"
msgstr "Dalam eksperimen hardware di [Bagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment), tiap ancilla check terhubung ke payload di beberapa titik sepanjang wire target dan diukur di *akhir Circuit* bersama qubit data, bukan di titik antara dengan reset dan pemakaian ulang. Sensitivitasnya tetap menjangkau *ke interior Circuit* karena operator check merambat melalui payload lewat konjugasi (dibahas di [Bagian 2.4](#paulice)). Yang kita tunjukkan adalah prinsip spacetime code, yaitu check yang daerah deteksinya menjangkau jauh ke interior Circuit, meskipun pengukuran terjadi di batas. Implementasi mid-circuit penuh (ukur, reset, pakai ulang) akan mengurangi lebih jauh waktu menganggur pada ancilla dan merupakan langkah rekayasa yang penting. Lihat [Lanes et al. (2025)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.20658) untuk bagaimana kemampuan dynamic circuit memungkinkan protokol ini dalam skala besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-4}"
msgstr "Uji pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding-4}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A 40-qubit circuit has post-selection rate $A = 0.6$ with one mid-circuit check. How many raw shots do you need to collect 3,000 accepted shots? What happens to this number if you add a second independent check with the same per-check post-selection rate?\n"
msgstr "Sebuah Circuit 40-qubit punya tingkat post-selection $A = 0.6$ dengan satu check di tengah Circuit. Berapa banyak raw shot yang kamu perlukan untuk mengumpulkan 3.000 shot yang diterima? Apa yang terjadi pada angka ini kalau kamu menambah check independen kedua dengan tingkat post-selection per check yang sama?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With one check at $A = 0.6$, the sampling overhead is $1/A \\approx 1.67$, so you need $3\\,000 / 0.6 = 5\\,000$ raw shots.\n"
msgstr "Dengan satu check pada $A = 0.6$, overhead sampling-nya $1/A \\approx 1.67$, jadi kamu butuh $3\\,000 / 0.6 = 5\\,000$ raw shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a second independent check also passes 60% of shots, the combined post-selection rate is $A_\\text{combined} = 0.6 \\times 0.6 = 0.36$. Now you need $3\\,000 / 0.36 \\approx 8\\,334$ raw shots, about $1.67\\times$ the single-check case.\n"
msgstr "Kalau check independen kedua juga meloloskan 60% shot, tingkat post-selection gabungannya $A_\\text{combined} = 0.6 \\times 0.6 = 0.36$. Sekarang kamu butuh $3\\,000 / 0.36 \\approx 8\\,334$ raw shot, sekitar $1.67\\times$ kasus satu check.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This illustrates that each additional check multiplies the sampling cost, which shows that adding checks is not free. The fidelity gain from each extra check needs to justify the additional loss in post-selection rate. [Section 2.5](#hardware-experiment) examines this trade-off in real hardware data.\n"
msgstr "Ini menunjukkan bahwa setiap check tambahan melipatgandakan biaya sampling, yang berarti menambah check itu tidak gratis. Peningkatan fidelity dari tiap check ekstra harus sepadan dengan tambahan kehilangan pada post-selection rate. [Bagian 2.5](#hardware-experiment) mengkaji trade-off ini pada data hardware nyata.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Note: this calculation assumes check outcomes are independent. In practice, checks may share sensitivity to the same noise sources, so the combined post-selection rate can differ from the simple product.)\n"
msgstr "(Catatan: perhitungan ini mengasumsikan hasil check saling independen. Dalam praktiknya, check bisa sama-sama sensitif terhadap sumber noise yang sama, sehingga tingkat post-selection gabungan bisa berbeda dari perkalian sederhana.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"<span id=\"coherent\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) {#22-coherent-pauli-checks-cpc}"
msgstr "2.2 Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) {#22-coherent-pauli-checks-cpc}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) provide a framework for what to check and why the check works.\n"
msgstr "Coherent Pauli checks (CPC) menyediakan kerangka kerja untuk apa yang dicek dan mengapa check itu bekerja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we have a Clifford circuit $U$ (the *payload*) that we want to protect. We pick a Pauli operator $R$ and apply it to the payload's output through a controlled-Pauli gate from an ancilla. The pre-payload partner $L$, obtained by pulling $R$ back through $U$, is applied to the input through a second controlled-Pauli. In the ideal (error-free) circuit the two controlled-Paulis cancel coherently on the ancilla, so the ancilla measurement is deterministic. Errors between the two controlled-Paulis that anti-commute with the effective check operator break this cancellation and can flip the ancilla outcome.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita punya Circuit Clifford $U$ (si *payload*) yang ingin kita lindungi. Kita pilih operator Pauli $R$ dan menerapkannya ke output payload lewat gate controlled-Pauli dari sebuah ancilla. Pasangan pra-payload $L$, yang didapat dengan menarik $R$ mundur melalui $U$, diterapkan ke input lewat controlled-Pauli kedua. Pada Circuit ideal (tanpa error), kedua controlled-Pauli saling meniadakan secara koheren pada ancilla, sehingga pengukuran ancilla bersifat deterministik. Error di antara kedua controlled-Pauli yang anti-komut dengan operator check efektif akan merusak pembatalan ini dan bisa membalik hasil ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Two ways the deterministic outcome can arise\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Dua cara hasil deterministik bisa muncul\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*State-preparation setting.* When $U$ is run on the standard input $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ and $R$ is chosen to be a stabilizer of the target output state $U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, then $R$ alone returns $+1$ on the ideal output. This is the case for the right-only checks in Section 2.3.3. An input stabilizer $Z_j$ pushed forward through the payload stabilizes the output state, so it returns $+1$ with no $L$ needed.\n"
msgstr "*Pengaturan persiapan state.* Ketika $U$ dijalankan pada input standar $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ dan $R$ dipilih sebagai stabilizer dari state output target $U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, maka $R$ saja sudah mengembalikan $+1$ pada output ideal. Inilah kasus check right-only di Bagian 2.3.3. Stabilizer input $Z_j$ yang didorong maju melalui payload menstabilkan state output, jadi ia mengembalikan $+1$ tanpa perlu $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*General CPC setting.* $R$ need *not* be a stabilizer by itself. The guarantee comes from the pair $(L, R)$: the coherent $L$-$U$-$R$ sandwich returns the ancilla to its starting value on an error-free circuit. If $R$ is not a stabilizer of the output, measuring it alone need not give a deterministic result. The *consistency* between $L$ and $R$ is checked, not the eigenvalue of either operator individually.\n"
msgstr "*Pengaturan CPC umum.* $R$ *tidak* harus menjadi stabilizer dengan sendirinya. Jaminannya datang dari pasangan $(L, R)$: sandwich koheren $L$-$U$-$R$ mengembalikan ancilla ke nilai awalnya pada Circuit tanpa error. Kalau $R$ bukan stabilizer dari output, mengukurnya saja belum tentu memberi hasil deterministik. Yang dicek adalah *konsistensi* antara $L$ dan $R$, bukan nilai eigen masing-masing operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In both settings the detection mechanism is the same.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada kedua pengaturan, mekanisme deteksinya sama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The detection mechanism is anti-commutation: an error anti-commuting with the check flips its outcome from $+1$ to $-1$, while an error commuting with the check passes undetected. (Concretely, $R = Z_0 Z_1$ catches $X$ or $Y$ on qubits 0-1 because $XZ = -ZX$, but misses $Z$-type errors there because $Z$ commutes with itself.)\n"
msgstr "Mekanisme deteksinya adalah anti-komutasi: error yang anti-komut dengan check membalik hasilnya dari $+1$ ke $-1$, sedangkan error yang komut dengan check lolos tanpa terdeteksi. (Konkretnya, $R = Z_0 Z_1$ menangkap $X$ atau $Y$ pada qubit 0-1 karena $XZ = -ZX$, tapi melewatkan error tipe-$Z$ di sana karena $Z$ komut dengan dirinya sendiri.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see what this looks like in practice, and why it creates a scalability challenge, we build an example step by step.\n"
msgstr "Untuk melihat seperti apa ini dalam praktik, dan mengapa ini menimbulkan tantangan skalabilitas, kita bangun sebuah contoh selangkah demi selangkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2.1 CPC in practice: the cost of conjugation {#221-cpc-in-practice-the-cost-of-conjugation}"
msgstr "2.2.1 CPC dalam praktik: biaya konjugasi {#221-cpc-in-practice-the-cost-of-conjugation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We build a 20-qubit random Clifford payload using a hardware-friendly Clifford gate set (H, CZ, SX, S). The circuit has a *brickwork structure*: alternating layers of nearest-neighbor CZ entangling gates, interleaved with random single-qubit Clifford gates (randomly chosen sequences of SX and S). The depth parameter counts CZ layers and we use five layers for the examples in Sections [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime). Its nearest-neighbor structure can be mapped to a physical line. [Section 2.4](#paulice) extends this construction to a deeper payload for the Paulice benchmark.\n"
msgstr "Kita bangun payload Clifford acak 20-qubit memakai set gate Clifford yang ramah hardware (H, CZ, SX, S). Circuit ini punya *struktur brickwork*: lapisan gate entangling CZ tetangga-terdekat yang bergantian, diselingi gate Clifford satu-qubit acak (urutan SX dan S yang dipilih acak). Parameter kedalaman menghitung lapisan CZ dan kita pakai lima lapisan untuk contoh di Bagian [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime). Struktur tetangga-terdekatnya bisa dipetakan ke sebuah garis fisik. [Bagian 2.4](#paulice) memperluas konstruksi ini ke payload yang lebih dalam untuk benchmark Paulice.\n"

