# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before transpilation the CPC adds only a small, fixed number of gates over the bare payload. After transpilation to the backend, the overhead concentrates in the two-qubit layers.  The two-qubit gate count rises, and the two-qubit depth, a useful indicator of accumulated noise, also grows. Part of this overhead is routing. A single ancilla has to reach the supports of both $L$ and $R$, so even the weight-2 $R$ coupling can need extra gates, and this full-circuit count does not separate the two contributions.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum transpilasi, CPC hanya menambah sejumlah kecil gate yang tetap di atas payload polos. Setelah transpilasi ke backend, overhead terkonsentrasi di lapisan dua-qubit. Jumlah gate dua-qubit naik, dan kedalaman dua-qubit, indikator yang berguna untuk akumulasi noise, juga bertambah. Sebagian overhead ini adalah routing. Satu ancilla harus menjangkau support $L$ dan $R$ sekaligus, jadi bahkan kopling $R$ berbobot-2 pun bisa butuh gate tambahan, dan jumlah Circuit penuh ini tidak memisahkan kedua kontribusi tersebut.\n"

