msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5 Hardware experiment: spacetime checks on the payload {#25-hardware-experiment-spacetime-checks-on-the-payload}"
msgstr "2.5 Eksperimen hardware: check spacetime pada payload {#25-hardware-experiment-spacetime-checks-on-the-payload}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Section 2.4](#paulice) used a device-based noise model to select and score checks. We now test on hardware whether post-selection brings the measured observables closer to their ideal values, and how many shots that improvement costs. Using the same ten-layer payload and fixed data line, we compare an unchecked baseline with an increasing number of checks. Following the [spacetime-code tutorial](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), we repeat the search for each sampled stabilizer and compare raw and post-selected expectation values alongside acceptance.\n"
msgstr "[Bagian 2.4](#paulice) memakai model noise berbasis device untuk memilih dan menilai check. Sekarang kita menguji di hardware apakah post-selection membuat observable yang terukur lebih dekat ke nilai idealnya, dan berapa banyak shot yang dibutuhkan untuk peningkatan itu. Dengan payload sepuluh-layer dan data line tetap yang sama, kita membandingkan baseline tanpa check dengan jumlah check yang makin banyak. Mengikuti [tutorial spacetime-code](/tutorials/spacetime-codes), kita mengulang pencarian untuk tiap stabilizer yang disampel dan membandingkan nilai ekspektasi mentah dan hasil post-selection beserta acceptance-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why sampled stabilizers? {#why-sampled-stabilizers}"
msgstr "Kenapa stabilizer yang disampel? {#why-sampled-stabilizers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payload prepares a stabilizer state $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, and its projector is the average of the $2^n$ signed elements of its stabilizer group, $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = 2^{-n} \\sum_G G$. The fidelity $\\langle\\psi|\\rho|\\psi\\rangle$ of a prepared state $\\rho$ is therefore the average of $\\langle G\\rangle_\\rho$ over a uniformly random stabilizer $G$, and every $G$ has ideal value $+1$. Measuring one $G$ needs only single-qubit rotations before readout, and its value in each shot is a sign times the parity of the measured bits on its support. A few sampled stabilizers give an estimate of the fidelity whose uncertainty shrinks with the number of samples, so the benchmark stays verifiable at any qubit count. Because the sampled stabilizers carry $X$ and $Y$ factors as well as $Z$, the estimate responds to phase errors as well as bit flips.\n"
msgstr "Payload menyiapkan state stabilizer $|\\psi\\rangle = U|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$, dan proyektornya adalah rata-rata dari $2^n$ elemen bertanda dari grup stabilizer-nya, $|\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi| = 2^{-n} \\sum_G G$. Karena itu fidelity $\\langle\\psi|\\rho|\\psi\\rangle$ dari state $\\rho$ yang disiapkan adalah rata-rata $\\langle G\\rangle_\\rho$ atas stabilizer $G$ yang dipilih acak seragam, dan setiap $G$ punya nilai ideal $+1$. Mengukur satu $G$ hanya memerlukan rotasi satu-qubit sebelum readout, dan nilainya di setiap shot adalah tanda dikali paritas bit terukur pada support-nya. Beberapa stabilizer yang disampel memberi estimasi fidelity yang ketidakpastiannya menyusut seiring jumlah sampel, sehingga benchmark tetap bisa diverifikasi pada jumlah qubit berapa pun. Karena stabilizer yang disampel membawa faktor $X$ dan $Y$ selain $Z$, estimasinya merespons phase error maupun bit flip.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"A note on the word &quot;fidelity&quot; in this section\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan soal kata &quot;fidelity&quot; di bagian ini\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the bare circuits (B0), the average of $\\langle G\\rangle$ over the sampled stabilizers estimates the fidelity of the prepared state. Ten samples give a rough estimate, whose uncertainty depends on both shot noise and variation between the sampled stabilizers. For the checked layouts it does not, even before post-selection. Their checks are chosen separately for every stabilizer, so the data need not be in the same state across the measurement settings. A check can preserve the ideal measurement statistics without preserving the full data state, as noted for the one-sided example. We therefore read both the raw and the post-selected averages of the checked layouts as benchmarks of expectation values, observable by observable, and not as the fidelity of one state.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk circuit tanpa check (B0), rata-rata $\\langle G\\rangle$ atas stabilizer yang disampel mengestimasi fidelity dari state yang disiapkan. Sepuluh sampel memberi estimasi kasar, yang ketidakpastiannya bergantung pada shot noise dan variasi antar stabilizer yang disampel. Untuk layout dengan check, hal ini tidak berlaku, bahkan sebelum post-selection. Check-nya dipilih terpisah untuk setiap stabilizer, jadi data belum tentu berada di state yang sama di seluruh pengaturan pengukuran. Sebuah check bisa mempertahankan statistik pengukuran ideal tanpa mempertahankan state data secara penuh, seperti yang dicatat pada contoh satu sisi. Karena itu kita membaca rata-rata mentah maupun hasil post-selection dari layout dengan check sebagai benchmark nilai ekspektasi, observable demi observable, dan bukan sebagai fidelity dari satu state.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To test how the number of checks affects detection performance, we compare a ladder of check counts on every sampled stabilizer. All layouts share the payload, the data line, and the measurement, and they differ only in how many checks they add.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menguji bagaimana jumlah check memengaruhi performa deteksi, kita membandingkan tangga jumlah check pada setiap stabilizer yang disampel. Semua layout berbagi payload, data line, dan pengukuran, dan hanya berbeda pada berapa banyak check yang mereka tambahkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.1 The layouts {#251-the-layouts}"
msgstr "2.5.1 Layout {#251-the-layouts}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For every sampled stabilizer $G$, `add_pauli_checks` runs the search of [Section 2.4](#paulice) on the circuit that measures $G$, with the targets in the order found there for $G_0$, from the best single check down. It commits one check per target and returns the circuit after each commitment, so one call per stabilizer gives the whole ladder. The important question is how many committed checks to keep.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap stabilizer $G$ yang disampel, `add_pauli_checks` menjalankan pencarian dari [Bagian 2.4](#paulice) pada circuit yang mengukur $G$, dengan target dalam urutan yang ditemukan di sana untuk $G_0$, dari single check terbaik ke bawah. Ia meng-commit satu check per target dan mengembalikan circuit setelah tiap commit, jadi satu panggilan per stabilizer menghasilkan seluruh tangga. Pertanyaan pentingnya adalah berapa banyak check yang di-commit yang perlu dipertahankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The layouts are B0, P1, P2, P4, and the last P layout: zero, one, two, and four committed checks, and all of them. The name gives the check count. The last layout keeps every check the search commits, as the tutorial does, and its count depends on how many data qubits have a usable free neighbor. Reading the ladder in order compares successive check-augmented implementations, with B0, the unchecked circuit returned by the search, as the control.\n"
msgstr "Layout-nya adalah B0, P1, P2, P4, dan layout P terakhir: nol, satu, dua, dan empat check yang di-commit, dan semuanya. Nama layout menunjukkan jumlah check. Layout terakhir mempertahankan setiap check yang di-commit pencarian, seperti di tutorial, dan jumlahnya bergantung pada berapa banyak data qubit yang punya tetangga bebas yang bisa dipakai. Membaca tangga secara berurutan membandingkan implementasi dengan check tambahan yang berurutan, dengan B0, circuit tanpa check yang dikembalikan pencarian, sebagai kontrol.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each $G$ gets its own checks, because the search depends on the measured observable. The selected data line, committed checks, gate counts, and model scores depend on the backend and its calibration. Use the tables generated by the current run as the reference, and compare the hardware results within that run.\n"
msgstr "Tiap $G$ mendapat check-nya sendiri, karena pencarian bergantung pada observable yang diukur. Data line yang dipilih, check yang di-commit, jumlah gate, dan skor model bergantung pada backend dan kalibrasinya. Pakai tabel yang dihasilkan oleh run saat ini sebagai acuan, dan bandingkan hasil hardware di dalam run tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Availability note\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Catatan ketersediaan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a data line with few usable free neighbors, the search commits fewer than four checks. P4 is then dropped and the last P layout keeps the checks as they are. If one stabilizer commits fewer checks than the others, the ladder stops at that smaller count for all of them.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada data line dengan sedikit tetangga bebas yang bisa dipakai, pencarian meng-commit kurang dari empat check. P4 lalu dihapus dan layout P terakhir mempertahankan check apa adanya. Jika satu stabilizer meng-commit lebih sedikit check daripada yang lain, tangga berhenti di jumlah yang lebih kecil itu untuk semuanya.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.2 Comparing layouts without running {#252-comparing-layouts-without-running}"
msgstr "2.5.2 Membandingkan layout tanpa menjalankannya {#252-comparing-layouts-without-running}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The table compares the layouts on two quantities available before any shot is taken, both averaged over the stabilizers. Compare gamma at each step with B0 and the preceding layout. A lower value indicates less uncovered noise under the model, and neither a monotonic decrease nor the highest value at B0 is guaranteed. The added two-qubit gates show the price. Each check couples its ancilla to its target at a few points, and because the ancilla is a neighbor of the target, no routing is needed.\n"
msgstr "Tabel membandingkan layout berdasarkan dua besaran yang tersedia sebelum shot apa pun diambil, keduanya dirata-ratakan atas stabilizer. Bandingkan gamma di tiap langkah dengan B0 dan layout sebelumnya. Nilai yang lebih rendah menunjukkan noise yang tidak tercakup lebih sedikit menurut model, dan tidak dijamin gamma turun secara monoton maupun bahwa nilai tertinggi ada di B0. Gate dua-qubit tambahan menunjukkan harganya. Tiap check menghubungkan ancilla-nya ke targetnya di beberapa titik, dan karena ancilla bertetangga dengan target, routing tidak diperlukan.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The addon models device noise as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad channel: a set of Pauli fault generators $P_k$, one per gate location and Pauli type, each with a rate $\\lambda_k$. For a two-qubit gate with calibrated error probability $p$, the error is split evenly over the 15 non-identity two-qubit Paulis, and each generator gets $\\lambda = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln(1 - 2p/15)$. Propagating operators through the circuit sorts the generators into three groups: those that commute with every measured operator (harmless, since they cannot change the output), those that anti-commute with some check's propagated support (detected, since they flip a syndrome bit), and the remainder, the uncovered faults within the measurement lightcone. Gamma is:\n"
msgstr "Addon memodelkan noise device sebagai kanal sparse Pauli-Lindblad: sekumpulan generator error Pauli $P_k$, satu per lokasi gate dan jenis Pauli, masing-masing dengan laju $\\lambda_k$. Untuk gate dua-qubit dengan probabilitas error terkalibrasi $p$, error dibagi rata ke 15 Pauli dua-qubit non-identitas, dan tiap generator mendapat $\\lambda = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\ln(1 - 2p/15)$. Mempropagasi operator lewat Circuit mengelompokkan generator ke dalam tiga grup: yang commute dengan setiap operator terukur (tidak berbahaya, karena tidak bisa mengubah output), yang anti-commute dengan support terpropagasi dari suatu check (terdeteksi, karena membalik bit syndrome), dan sisanya, yaitu error yang tidak tercakup di dalam lightcone pengukuran. Gamma adalah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\gamma = \\exp\\Big(2 \\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\text{uncovered}} \\lambda_k\\Big),$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\gamma = \\exp\\Big(2 \\sum_{k\\,\\in\\,\\text{uncovered}} \\lambda_k\\Big),$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the quasi-probability cost of the channel that would invert exactly that residual noise ([van den Berg, Minev, Kandala, and Temme, Nat. Phys. 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)). For this convention, the usual PEC sampling cost scales as $\\gamma^2$, while post-selection has a separate acceptance cost $1/A$. $\\gamma = 1$ means no positive-rate generator remains uncovered within the measurement lightcone. Committing a check that covers generators of total rate $\\Lambda$ divides gamma by $e^{2\\Lambda}$, while the generators of the check's own gates that it leaves undetected multiply gamma back up. This multiplicative structure is why each well-placed check lowers gamma by its own factor, and why a check that adds more noise than it covers can raise it.\n"
msgstr "biaya quasi-probabilitas dari kanal yang akan membalikkan persis noise residual tersebut ([van den Berg, Minev, Kandala, and Temme, Nat. Phys. 2023](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866)). Untuk konvensi ini, biaya sampling PEC yang biasa berskala $\\gamma^2$, sedangkan post-selection punya biaya acceptance terpisah $1/A$. $\\gamma = 1$ berarti tidak ada generator berlaju positif yang tersisa tanpa tercakup di dalam lightcone pengukuran. Meng-commit sebuah check yang mencakup generator dengan laju total $\\Lambda$ membagi gamma dengan $e^{2\\Lambda}$, sedangkan generator dari gate milik check itu sendiri yang tidak terdeteksi mengalikan gamma kembali naik. Struktur perkalian ini menjelaskan kenapa tiap check yang ditempatkan dengan baik menurunkan gamma dengan faktornya sendiri, dan kenapa check yang menambah lebih banyak noise daripada yang dicakupnya bisa menaikkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the exponent accumulates hundreds of generator rates, absolute gamma is exponentially sensitive to the calibration scale. A modest change in the per-gate error rate raises gamma to a power, so values can differ substantially between backends and between calibration days. Compare gammas only within a single run on a single backend, where the ordering is what matters. When a linear, additive quantity is needed, use $\\ln\\gamma / 2 = \\sum_k \\lambda_k$, the uncovered rate budget; each check's contribution then reads off as a difference of $\\ln\\gamma$.\n"
msgstr "Karena eksponen mengakumulasi ratusan laju generator, gamma absolut sangat sensitif secara eksponensial terhadap skala kalibrasi. Perubahan kecil pada laju error per gate menaikkan gamma ke suatu pangkat, jadi nilainya bisa berbeda jauh antar backend dan antar hari kalibrasi. Bandingkan gamma hanya di dalam satu run pada satu backend, di mana urutannya yang penting. Saat butuh besaran linear dan aditif, pakai $\\ln\\gamma / 2 = \\sum_k \\lambda_k$, anggaran laju yang tidak tercakup; kontribusi tiap check lalu terbaca sebagai selisih $\\ln\\gamma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise model comes from `PauliceNoiseModel.from_backend(backend, data_line)`. Each data-line coupler keeps its own calibrated error, readout enters as the average over the data line, and the couplers a check adds get a typical rate, which is why [Section 2.4](#paulice) screens the actual ancilla couplers against the calibration.\n"
msgstr "Model noise berasal dari `PauliceNoiseModel.from_backend(backend, data_line)`. Tiap coupler data-line mempertahankan error terkalibrasinya sendiri, readout masuk sebagai rata-rata atas data line, dan coupler yang ditambahkan check mendapat laju tipikal, itulah sebabnya [Bagian 2.4](#paulice) menyaring coupler ancilla yang sebenarnya terhadap kalibrasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.3 Hardware results {#253-hardware-results}"
msgstr "2.5.3 Hasil hardware {#253-hardware-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The addon inserts its checks on the transpiled circuit, so it returns each layout as a ready-to-run [ISA circuit](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture): payload, check ancillas, and measurements, already placed on physical qubits. Every circuit therefore goes to hardware exactly as scored, with no further transpilation (because re-routing would move the checks off the qubits the search chose). Submit all circuits in one job and wait for completion before proceeding.\n"
msgstr "Addon menyisipkan check-nya pada circuit yang sudah di-transpile, jadi ia mengembalikan tiap layout sebagai [ISA circuit](/guides/transpile#instruction-set-architecture) siap jalan: payload, ancilla check, dan pengukuran, yang sudah ditempatkan pada qubit fisik. Karena itu setiap circuit dikirim ke hardware persis seperti saat dinilai, tanpa transpilation lagi (karena routing ulang akan memindahkan check dari qubit yang dipilih pencarian). Kirim semua circuit dalam satu job dan tunggu sampai selesai sebelum melanjutkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The submitted circuits retain their check rules, sampled stabilizers, and model scores in metadata. When retrieving a job, use these saved definitions. Repeating the search can change the checks and must not change how an earlier job is analyzed.\n"
msgstr "Circuit yang dikirim menyimpan aturan check, stabilizer yang disampel, dan skor model di metadata. Saat mengambil job, pakai definisi yang tersimpan ini. Mengulang pencarian bisa mengubah check dan tidak boleh mengubah cara job sebelumnya dianalisis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following explains how the post-selection works. Each circuit measures the data qubits into register `meas` and the check ancillas into register `checks_c`. Each check contributes one syndrome bit per shot, the XOR of the measured bits of the qubits in its `check_support`; `0` means the comparison came out clean and `1` means the check fired. `cc.get_postselection_method()` returns the rule that reads this record. We rebuild it from the check definitions and the register and measurement map saved with each circuit, then pass it the bitstring from `join_data()` in that circuit's register order, and a shot is kept only when no check fired. The value of $G$ in a shot is its sign times the parity of the data bits on its support, as described above.\n"
msgstr "Berikut penjelasan cara kerja post-selection. Tiap circuit mengukur data qubit ke register `meas` dan ancilla check ke register `checks_c`. Tiap check menyumbang satu bit syndrome per shot, yaitu XOR dari bit terukur qubit di `check_support`-nya; `0` berarti perbandingan keluar bersih dan `1` berarti check menyala. `cc.get_postselection_method()` mengembalikan aturan yang membaca catatan ini. Kita membangunnya ulang dari definisi check serta register dan peta pengukuran yang disimpan bersama tiap circuit, lalu memberinya bitstring dari `join_data()` dalam urutan register circuit tersebut, dan sebuah shot hanya dipertahankan jika tidak ada check yang menyala. Nilai $G$ dalam sebuah shot adalah tandanya dikali paritas bit data pada support-nya, seperti dijelaskan di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The table reports the following metrics for each layout:\n"
msgstr "Tabel melaporkan metrik berikut untuk tiap layout:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Column | Meaning |\n"
"|:-------|:--------|\n"
"| `layout` | B0 has no checks; P1, P2, P4, and the last P layout hold that many committed checks |\n"
"| `checks` | Number of checks per circuit |\n"
"| `gamma` | The addon's residual-noise cancellation cost estimate from Section 2.5.2 |\n"
"| `added 2Q gates` | Two-qubit gates added to the unchecked circuit |\n"
"| `A` | *Post-selection rate*: fraction of shots passing all checks (1.0 = no checks) |\n"
"| `1/A` | *Sampling overhead*: how many raw shots are needed per accepted shot |\n"
"| `raw` | Mean signed $\\langle G\\rangle$ over all shots, before post-selection |\n"
"| `post` | Mean signed $\\langle G\\rangle$ over the accepted shots only |\n"
"| `raw_ci`, `post_ci` | 95% half-widths from shot noise, for this fixed set of stabilizers |\n"
"| `gain vs B0` | `post` minus the `raw` value of B0 for the same stabilizer |\n"
"| `gain_se` | Standard error of that gain across the sampled stabilizers |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Kolom | Arti |\n"
"|:-------|:--------|\n"
"| `layout` | B0 tanpa check; P1, P2, P4, dan layout P terakhir memuat check yang di-commit sebanyak itu |\n"
"| `checks` | Jumlah check per circuit |\n"
"| `gamma` | Estimasi biaya pembatalan noise residual dari addon, dari Bagian 2.5.2 |\n"
"| `added 2Q gates` | Gate dua-qubit yang ditambahkan ke circuit tanpa check |\n"
"| `A` | *Post-selection rate*: fraksi shot yang lolos semua check (1.0 = tanpa check) |\n"
"| `1/A` | *Sampling overhead*: berapa banyak shot mentah yang dibutuhkan per shot yang diterima |\n"
"| `raw` | Rata-rata $\\langle G\\rangle$ bertanda atas semua shot, sebelum post-selection |\n"
"| `post` | Rata-rata $\\langle G\\rangle$ bertanda hanya atas shot yang diterima |\n"
"| `raw_ci`, `post_ci` | Setengah-lebar 95% dari shot noise, untuk himpunan stabilizer tetap ini |\n"
"| `gain vs B0` | `post` dikurangi nilai `raw` B0 untuk stabilizer yang sama |\n"
"| `gain_se` | Standard error dari gain tersebut atas stabilizer yang disampel |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rates and values are averaged over the ten sampled stabilizers; `1/A` uses the averaged `A`.\n"
msgstr "Laju dan nilai dirata-ratakan atas sepuluh stabilizer yang disampel; `1/A` memakai `A` yang dirata-ratakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the table along the check count, and compare the following two things measured on hardware:\n"
msgstr "Baca tabel sepanjang jumlah check, dan bandingkan dua hal berikut yang terukur di hardware:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*1. Whether the post-selected value improves, and at what cost in post-selection rate.* Each added check can cover more faults, but it also adds gates, and the search commits the best check it finds for each target in turn, even when that check raises gamma. Neither `post` nor gamma is guaranteed to improve at every step, so compare each change in `post` with the measured `A` and the uncertainty of the gain.\n"
msgstr "*1. Apakah nilai hasil post-selection membaik, dan berapa biayanya dalam post-selection rate.* Tiap check tambahan bisa mencakup lebih banyak error, tetapi juga menambah gate, dan pencarian meng-commit check terbaik yang ditemukannya untuk tiap target secara berurutan, bahkan ketika check itu menaikkan gamma. Baik `post` maupun gamma tidak dijamin membaik di setiap langkah, jadi bandingkan tiap perubahan `post` dengan `A` yang terukur dan ketidakpastian gain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*2. How the raw value changes as checks are added.* The added gates can introduce errors, so compare both `raw` and `post` with the raw value of B0. A gain over the checked layout's own raw value is not enough by itself to establish a benefit over running the bare circuit.\n"
msgstr "*2. Bagaimana nilai mentah berubah saat check ditambahkan.* Gate tambahan bisa menimbulkan error, jadi bandingkan `raw` maupun `post` dengan nilai mentah B0. Gain terhadap nilai mentah milik layout dengan check itu sendiri belum cukup untuk menunjukkan manfaat dibanding menjalankan circuit tanpa check.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, raw means decrease along the check ladder, while all post-selected point estimates exceed B0. The checked circuits therefore start from lower raw values, and the improvement appears after filtering. Compare the paired gains and their uncertainty before judging the benefit of each layout.\n"
msgstr "Pada run yang disimpan, rata-rata mentah menurun sepanjang tangga check, sementara semua estimasi titik hasil post-selection melebihi B0. Circuit dengan check karena itu mulai dari nilai mentah yang lebih rendah, dan peningkatannya muncul setelah penyaringan. Bandingkan gain berpasangan dan ketidakpastiannya sebelum menilai manfaat tiap layout.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/31ee3295-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-correction-i/extracted-outputs/31ee3295-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the left panel, faded bars show the raw mean of $\\langle G\\rangle$, solid bars show the post-selected mean, and the dashed line marks the bare baseline. The right panel shows the trade-off between post-selected mean and acceptance.\n"
msgstr "Di panel kiri, batang pudar menunjukkan rata-rata mentah $\\langle G\\rangle$, batang solid menunjukkan rata-rata hasil post-selection, dan garis putus-putus menandai baseline tanpa check. Panel kanan menunjukkan trade-off antara rata-rata hasil post-selection dan acceptance.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the saved run, the post-selected mean rises along the check ladder while acceptance falls. The layout with all committed checks gives the highest post-selected mean and the lowest accepted-shot yield. This ordering agrees with decreasing gamma in the model table, but it does not establish which layout is best for every application.\n"
msgstr "Pada run yang disimpan, rata-rata hasil post-selection naik sepanjang tangga check sementara acceptance turun. Layout dengan semua check yang di-commit memberi rata-rata hasil post-selection tertinggi dan yield shot diterima terendah. Urutan ini sesuai dengan gamma yang menurun di tabel model, tetapi tidak menetapkan layout mana yang terbaik untuk setiap aplikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gamma is a model score computed without experimental shots, not a guarantee of hardware performance. Agreement gives a rough check of its ranking for these sampled observables, and another backend or calibration can produce a different ordering. Compare the gain, its uncertainty, acceptance, and added circuit cost when choosing a layout.\n"
msgstr "Gamma adalah skor model yang dihitung tanpa shot eksperimen, bukan jaminan performa hardware. Kesesuaian memberi pengecekan kasar atas peringkatnya untuk observable yang disampel ini, dan backend atau kalibrasi lain bisa menghasilkan urutan berbeda. Bandingkan gain, ketidakpastiannya, acceptance, dan biaya circuit tambahan saat memilih layout.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5.4 Interpretation {#254-interpretation}"
msgstr "2.5.4 Interpretasi {#254-interpretation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The saved run illustrates the central trade-off of post-selected QEC: accepting fewer shots can improve agreement with the ideal observable values. Every checked layout improves on its own raw mean, and the all-check layout gives the largest post-selected gain over B0. Every checked raw mean is below B0 in this run, so the improvement over bare appears only after filtering.\n"
msgstr "Run yang disimpan menggambarkan trade-off utama dari QEC dengan post-selection: menerima lebih sedikit shot bisa memperbaiki kesesuaian dengan nilai observable ideal. Setiap layout dengan check membaik dibanding rata-rata mentahnya sendiri, dan layout dengan semua check memberi gain hasil post-selection terbesar atas B0. Setiap rata-rata mentah layout dengan check berada di bawah B0 pada run ini, jadi peningkatan di atas circuit tanpa check baru muncul setelah penyaringan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the same principle used in the spacetime-code demonstration cited in the introduction, but that demonstration's tenfold figure concerns effective gate error rates. Our observable-by-observable benchmark measures a different quantity and does not reproduce that numerical claim.\n"
msgstr "Ini prinsip yang sama dengan demonstrasi spacetime-code yang dikutip di pendahuluan, tetapi angka sepuluh kali lipat dari demonstrasi itu menyangkut laju error gate efektif. Benchmark observable demi observable kita mengukur besaran yang berbeda dan tidak mereproduksi klaim numerik tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report acceptance $A$ alongside the post-selected mean and the uncertainty of the paired gain. The sampling overhead $1/A$ and added gates determine the cost of obtaining accepted shots; more checks need not improve that trade-off. Both the values and their ordering can change with backend calibration, and the model's gamma ranking need not match the hardware ranking.\n"
msgstr "Laporkan acceptance $A$ bersama rata-rata hasil post-selection dan ketidakpastian gain berpasangan. Sampling overhead $1/A$ dan gate tambahan menentukan biaya memperoleh shot yang diterima; lebih banyak check belum tentu memperbaiki trade-off itu. Nilai maupun urutannya bisa berubah seiring kalibrasi backend, dan peringkat gamma dari model belum tentu cocok dengan peringkat hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-7}"
msgstr "Cek pemahamanmu {#check-your-understanding-7}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two layouts use the same qubit layout. One has no checks (acceptance rate = 1.0); the other has multiple checks (lower acceptance rate). The checked layout shows a higher post-selected value of $\\langle G\\rangle$. Which layout is better?\n"
msgstr "Dua layout memakai layout qubit yang sama. Satu tanpa check (acceptance rate = 1.0); yang lain punya beberapa check (acceptance rate lebih rendah). Layout dengan check menunjukkan nilai $\\langle G\\rangle$ hasil post-selection yang lebih tinggi. Layout mana yang lebih baik?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*It depends on the application.*\n"
msgstr "*Tergantung aplikasinya.*\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the goal is accurate individual samples, for example in sampling-based algorithms where each accepted shot is a single-shot output, the checked layout might be preferable. Its accepted shots agree more often with the ideal value of the measured observable, and each kept shot is a sample, not a statistical reconstruction. This single-shot property is what distinguishes error detection from error mitigation. A higher post-selected $\\langle G\\rangle$ alone does not show that each accepted shot comes from a higher-fidelity state, because a check can change the data state without changing the statistics of $G$.\n"
msgstr "Jika tujuannya sampel individual yang akurat, misalnya pada algoritma berbasis sampling di mana tiap shot yang diterima adalah output single-shot, layout dengan check mungkin lebih disukai. Shot yang diterimanya lebih sering sesuai dengan nilai ideal dari observable yang diukur, dan tiap shot yang dipertahankan adalah sebuah sampel, bukan rekonstruksi statistik. Properti single-shot inilah yang membedakan error detection dari error mitigation. $\\langle G\\rangle$ hasil post-selection yang lebih tinggi saja tidak menunjukkan bahwa tiap shot yang diterima berasal dari state dengan fidelity lebih tinggi, karena sebuah check bisa mengubah state data tanpa mengubah statistik $G$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the goal is many samples quickly and lower per-shot accuracy is acceptable (for example, for estimating expectation values), the unchecked layout may be more practical, because it produces more usable shots from the same batch.\n"
msgstr "Jika tujuannya banyak sampel dengan cepat dan akurasi per shot yang lebih rendah bisa diterima (misalnya, untuk mengestimasi nilai ekspektasi), layout tanpa check mungkin lebih praktis, karena menghasilkan lebih banyak shot yang bisa dipakai dari batch yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*A useful shorthand for comparing layouts.* A layout with post-selection rate $A$ keeps about $A N$ of $N$ raw shots, so it needs $1/A$ times as many raw shots for the same number of accepted shots. Equal accepted counts give equal precision only if the observable's variance among the accepted shots is also similar. Set that cost against the gap between the post-selected value and the raw value of the bare layout. Comparing layouts on both numbers illustrates that more checks do not always win.\n"
msgstr "*Singkatan yang berguna untuk membandingkan layout.* Layout dengan post-selection rate $A$ mempertahankan sekitar $A N$ dari $N$ shot mentah, jadi ia butuh $1/A$ kali lebih banyak shot mentah untuk jumlah shot diterima yang sama. Jumlah shot diterima yang sama memberi presisi yang sama hanya jika varians observable di antara shot yang diterima juga mirip. Timbang biaya itu terhadap selisih antara nilai hasil post-selection dan nilai mentah layout tanpa check. Membandingkan layout pada kedua angka ini menunjukkan bahwa lebih banyak check tidak selalu menang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Caveat: error detection is not unbiased.*\n"
msgstr "*Catatan: error detection tidak unbiased.*\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-selection removes the errors the checks detect, but not all errors. Faults that commute with every check or that occur outside any check's detection region pass through undetected. The post-selected distribution therefore remains *biased*: post-selection can reduce the bias, but it guarantees neither an improvement nor its complete removal. For tasks that require unbiased estimates of observables, error detection has to be combined with other error mitigation techniques (for example, probabilistic error cancellation on the post-selected data). The three relevant axes are:\n"
msgstr "Post-selection menghilangkan error yang dideteksi check, tetapi tidak semua error. Error yang commute dengan setiap check atau yang terjadi di luar detection region mana pun lolos tanpa terdeteksi. Distribusi hasil post-selection karena itu tetap *bias*: post-selection bisa mengurangi bias, tetapi tidak menjamin perbaikan maupun penghilangan sepenuhnya. Untuk tugas yang memerlukan estimasi observable yang unbiased, error detection harus dikombinasikan dengan teknik error mitigation lain (misalnya, probabilistic error cancellation pada data hasil post-selection). Tiga sumbu yang relevan adalah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Bias*: detection can reduce it, with no guarantee of a reduction or of its complete removal;\n"
msgstr "*Bias*: deteksi bisa menguranginya, tanpa jaminan pengurangan maupun penghilangan sepenuhnya;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Variance*: at comparable per-shot variance, fewer accepted shots mean higher statistical noise per estimate;\n"
msgstr "*Varians*: pada varians per shot yang sebanding, shot diterima yang lebih sedikit berarti noise statistik per estimasi lebih tinggi;\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Cost*: checks add gates, and rejected shots reduce the usable yield.\n"
msgstr "*Biaya*: check menambah gate, dan shot yang ditolak mengurangi yield yang bisa dipakai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design must consider all three of these.\n"
msgstr "Desain harus mempertimbangkan ketiganya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wrap-up {#wrap-up}"
msgstr "Penutup {#wrap-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson covered error detection in quantum circuits through two complementary approaches that differ in where and how checks are placed. Part 1 focused on end-of-circuit detection (checks applied after the circuit completes), while Part 2 developed mid-circuit detection (checks placed at interior points during circuit execution).\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini membahas error detection pada circuit kuantum lewat dua pendekatan yang saling melengkapi dan berbeda dalam di mana dan bagaimana check ditempatkan. Bagian 1 berfokus pada deteksi di akhir circuit (check diterapkan setelah circuit selesai), sedangkan Bagian 2 mengembangkan deteksi mid-circuit (check ditempatkan di titik-titik interior selama eksekusi circuit).\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Part 1: End-of-circuit detection* demonstrated two strategies. Symmetry post-selection ([Section 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) uses known output constraints, like GHZ's two-bitstring support, to filter corrupted shots in classical post-processing, requiring no extra qubits but only catching errors visible in the final measurement basis. Stabilizer-code post-selection ([Section 1.2](#stabilizer-code)) adds ancilla qubits and syndrome extraction at the circuit's end, detecting both bit-flip and phase-flip errors through the $[[4,2,2]]$ code. The key limitation: all check information is collected at the final boundary, so the syndrome cannot localize when or where faults occurred during execution.\n"
msgstr "*Bagian 1: Deteksi di akhir Circuit* menunjukkan dua strategi. Symmetry post-selection ([Bagian 1.1](#symmetry-post-selection)) memakai batasan output yang diketahui, seperti support dua-bitstring GHZ, untuk menyaring shot yang rusak dalam post-processing klasik, tidak memerlukan qubit tambahan tetapi hanya menangkap error yang terlihat di basis pengukuran akhir. Stabilizer-code post-selection ([Bagian 1.2](#stabilizer-code)) menambahkan ancilla qubit dan ekstraksi syndrome di akhir Circuit, mendeteksi error bit-flip maupun phase-flip lewat kode $[[4,2,2]]$. Keterbatasan utamanya: semua informasi check dikumpulkan di batas akhir, jadi syndrome tidak bisa melokalisasi kapan atau di mana error terjadi selama eksekusi.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Part 2: Mid-circuit detection* moved checks inside the circuit to access errors as they happen. Throughout, mid-circuit refers to where a check's detection region reaches, the circuit interior; the ancillas themselves are read out at the end alongside the data, with no dynamic-circuit operations. Coherent Pauli checks (Sections [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)) provided the algebraic foundation: for any Clifford circuit $U$, the relation $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ defines valid check pairs, with detection via anti-commutation. The 20-qubit random Clifford payload provides a benchmark for testing whether the detection benefit outweighs the noise from added gates and routing. Spacetime codes (Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)) refined this by placing lightweight checks where the circuit structure naturally supports them, with no $L$ needed, and tracing each check's *detection region* backward through the circuit. The `qiskit-paulice` addon automates that search and ranks placements by their model cost for residual noise. Sections [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment) use a deeper version of the same circuit construction and compare checks through sampled stabilizers, weighing the post-selected gain of each added check against the acceptance it costs.\n"
msgstr "*Bagian 2: Deteksi mid-circuit* memindahkan check ke dalam Circuit untuk menangkap error saat terjadi. Sepanjang bagian ini, mid-circuit merujuk pada sejauh mana detection region sebuah check menjangkau, yaitu interior Circuit; ancilla sendiri dibaca di akhir bersama data, tanpa operasi dynamic-circuit. Check Pauli koheren (Bagian [2.2](#coherent)-[2.3](#spacetime)) menyediakan fondasi aljabar: untuk Circuit Clifford $U$ apa pun, relasi $L = U^\\dagger R\\, U$ mendefinisikan pasangan check yang valid, dengan deteksi lewat anti-commutation. Payload Clifford acak 20-qubit menyediakan benchmark untuk menguji apakah manfaat deteksi mengimbangi noise dari gate dan routing tambahan. Spacetime code (Bagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment)) menyempurnakan ini dengan menempatkan check ringan di tempat struktur Circuit mendukungnya secara alami, tanpa perlu $L$, dan menelusuri *detection region* tiap check mundur melewati Circuit. Addon `qiskit-paulice` mengotomatiskan pencarian itu dan meranking penempatan berdasarkan biaya modelnya untuk noise residual. Bagian [2.4](#paulice)-[2.5](#hardware-experiment) memakai versi lebih dalam dari konstruksi Circuit yang sama dan membandingkan check lewat stabilizer yang disampel, menimbang gain hasil post-selection dari tiap check tambahan terhadap acceptance yang dikorbankannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson intentionally does not apply error mitigation or suppression techniques (for example, dynamical decoupling, readout error mitigation, or ZNE) that could further improve the results. The goal is to isolate the effect of error *detection* alone. Martiel & Javadi-Abhari report fidelity gains up to 236$\\times$ in their spacetime-check experiments, which also use dynamical decoupling and readout folding.\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini sengaja tidak menerapkan teknik error mitigation atau suppression (misalnya, dynamical decoupling, readout error mitigation, atau ZNE) yang bisa memperbaiki hasil lebih jauh. Tujuannya adalah mengisolasi efek dari error *detection* saja. Martiel & Javadi-Abhari melaporkan peningkatan fidelity hingga 236$\\times$ dalam eksperimen spacetime-check mereka, yang juga memakai dynamical decoupling dan readout folding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Limitations to consider.*\n"
msgstr "*Keterbatasan yang perlu dipertimbangkan.*\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spacetime checks are a *heuristic*. They do not catch all errors. Faults that commute with every check, or that occur outside any detection region, pass undetected. Post-selection can therefore reduce the bias of the results, but it guarantees neither an improvement nor the removal of every error. For unbiased estimation of observables, error detection should be combined with other quantum error mitigation techniques ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. I](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"
msgstr "Check spacetime adalah sebuah *heuristik*. Mereka tidak menangkap semua error. Error yang commute dengan setiap check, atau yang terjadi di luar detection region mana pun, lolos tanpa terdeteksi. Post-selection karena itu bisa mengurangi bias hasil, tetapi tidak menjamin perbaikan maupun penghilangan setiap error. Untuk estimasi observable yang unbiased, error detection sebaiknya dikombinasikan dengan teknik quantum error mitigation lain ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. I](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The checks are most effective for *Clifford-dominated circuits*; the space of valid checks shrinks exponentially with non-Clifford content ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"
msgstr "Check paling efektif untuk *circuit yang didominasi Clifford*; ruang check yang valid menyusut secara eksponensial seiring muatan non-Clifford ([Martiel & Javadi-Abhari, Supp. V](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.15725)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-22
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Pauli operator's overall phase becomes a *relative phase between the ancilla branches* when the operator is controlled, and may need compensation by a single-qubit gate on the ancilla wire. The one-sided example of Section 2.3.2 corrects a minus sign on $L$ this way, and general implementations must account for it.\n"
msgstr "Fase keseluruhan dari sebuah operator Pauli menjadi *fase relatif antar cabang ancilla* ketika operator tersebut dikontrol, dan mungkin perlu dikompensasi oleh gate satu-qubit pada wire ancilla. Contoh satu sisi di Bagian 2.3.2 mengoreksi tanda minus pada $L$ dengan cara ini, dan implementasi umum harus memperhitungkannya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-22
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three concrete open directions follow from this lesson. First, Sections [2.4](#paulice) and [2.5](#hardware-experiment) apply the placement search to a ten-layer 20-qubit payload; how its runtime scales to deeper circuits on hundreds of qubits determines whether the approach is practical for larger utility-scale circuits. Second, Part 2 used a random Clifford circuit construction at two depths. A natural next step is to check how the detection benefit holds up on deeper circuits and on circuits with some non-Clifford content, such as QAOA or VQE ansatze. Third, spacetime codes here use syndrome information for post-selection rather than active correction, and their heuristic construction has no particular distance guarantee. Moving to fault-tolerant correction requires checks with suitable distance, fault-tolerant syndrome extraction, and a decoder.\n"
msgstr "Ada tiga arah terbuka yang konkret dari pelajaran ini. Pertama, Bagian [2.4](#paulice) dan [2.5](#hardware-experiment) menerapkan pencarian penempatan pada payload 20-qubit dengan sepuluh layer; bagaimana runtime-nya berskala ke Circuit yang lebih dalam pada ratusan qubit menentukan apakah pendekatan ini praktis untuk Circuit skala utilitas yang lebih besar. Kedua, Bagian 2 memakai konstruksi Circuit Clifford acak pada dua kedalaman. Langkah lanjutan yang wajar adalah memeriksa seberapa baik manfaat deteksi bertahan pada Circuit yang lebih dalam dan pada Circuit dengan sedikit konten non-Clifford, seperti ansatz QAOA atau VQE. Ketiga, spacetime code di sini memakai informasi syndrome untuk post-selection, bukan koreksi aktif, dan konstruksi heuristiknya tidak punya jaminan jarak tertentu. Untuk beralih ke koreksi fault-tolerant, dibutuhkan check dengan jarak yang sesuai, ekstraksi syndrome fault-tolerant, dan sebuah decoder.\n"

